Article 782. Information on continuous airworthiness
Operators of aircraft with an approved maximum takeoff weight of more than 5,700 kg or of helicopters with an approved maximum takeoff weight of more than 3,175 kg must establish procedures for receiving, evaluating and implementing information, directives and requirements on maintaining continuous airworthiness issued by the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam, the country of registration (if not Vietnam) and the organization responsible for the type design, including:
1. Receive, evaluate and monitor information, directives and requirements on maintaining continuous airworthiness.
2. Take timely actions necessary to maintain continued airworthiness in accordance with the regulations of the country of registration.
3. Provide information and reports as required by the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam or the country of registration (if not Vietnam).
4. Collect, analyze and respond to operational information related to continuous airworthiness as required by the organization responsible for the type design, the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam or the country of registration (if not Vietnam)."},"translatedText":"Article 782. Information on continuous airworthiness

Article 782. Information on continuous airworthiness
