Article 787. Training program for maintenance control staff and maintenance of airworthiness standards of aircraft operators
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for developing, promulgating and organizing the implementation of training programs for controllers qualified to continuously fly and maintenance management staff.
2. The training program must be consistent with assigned tasks and ensure that employees have sufficient knowledge, skills and abilities to perform maintenance control work and maintain aircraft airworthiness standards including.;
a) Knowledge of Vietnam's civil aviation legal system; standards and technical regulations; requirements, procedures and guidance documents related to maintenance management, maintenance control, and maintenance of continuous airworthiness standards of aircraft;
b) Maintenance control system, aircraft maintenance program and applicable procedures of the Operator;
c) Safety management system (SMS), technical risk management, human factors and measures to prevent incidents during aircraft operation and maintenance;
d) Periodic training on updating airworthiness standards, new technology, inspection procedures and safety recommendations of ICAO, aircraft manufacturers, national design authorities and the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam.
d) Failure control procedures, applying MEL/CDL, controlling aircraft configuration and implementing airworthiness orders
3. Aircraft operators must conduct initial training, periodic training and updated training when there are changes in regulations, technical standards, aircraft types or applicable operation and maintenance procedures.
4. Aircraft operators must periodically review and update training programs to ensure compliance with changes in international regulations and standards.
5. Employees are only allowed to perform independent tasks when they have completed the training program, have been assessed as satisfactory, and have been confirmed by the aircraft operator to be competent in accordance with the assigned tasks.
