i) Hướng dẫn an toàn cho hành khách, bao gồm cả thông tin về vị trí và cách sử dụng các trang thiết bị không thể hiện trong bảng hướng dẫn an toàn của người khai thác tàu bay, như bình chữa cháy, thiết bị sơ cứu (bộ sơ cứu, máy khử rung tim), mặt nạ khói và các thiết bị khác;
k) Các hướng dẫn an toàn bổ sung khác khi cần thiết để bảo đảm an toàn cho hành khách.</p>","translations":{"en":"Article 791. General aviation operating procedures do not arrange flight attendants on aircraft with the maximum approved passenger seat configuration greater than 19 and the actual number of passengers not exceeding 19 people.

Article 791. General aviation operating procedures do not arrange flight attendants on aircraft with the maximum approved passenger seat configuration greater than 19 and the actual number of passengers not exceeding 19 people.
1. Aircraft operators must conduct a risk assessment for operating flights without flight attendants and ensure that an equivalent level of safety is maintained for passengers on the aircraft.
2. Flight crew members assigned to flights must be trained in operations without flight attendants.
3. Aircraft operators must consider the characteristics and capabilities of passengers on the flight, including the level of knowledge of the aircraft type and procedures under normal, abnormal and emergency conditions.
4. The exploitation process must include the following contents:
a) Communication and coordination between crew and passengers;
b) Handling cases where flight crew members are unable to perform their duties;
c) Monitor the passenger compartment;
d) Organize quick escape from the aircraft in case of necessity;
d) Operate and use emergency exits and emergency escape aids;
e) Location and use of oxygen equipment;
g) Location and use of life jackets;
h) Arrange passenger seating to ensure easy access to emergency exits, maintain timely communication with the flight crew and ensure the mass and balance limits of the aircraft;
i) Safety instructions for passengers, including information on the location and use of equipment not shown in the aircraft operator's safety instructions, such as fire extinguishers, first aid equipment (first aid kit, defibrillator), smoke masks and other equipment;
k) Other additional safety instructions when necessary to ensure passenger safety."},"translatedText":"Article 791. General aviation operating procedures do not arrange flight attendants on aircraft with the maximum approved passenger seat configuration greater than 19 and the actual number of passengers not exceeding 19 people.

Article 791. General aviation operating procedures do not arrange flight attendants on aircraft with the maximum approved passenger seat configuration greater than 19 and the actual number of passengers not exceeding 19 people.
1. Aircraft operators must conduct a risk assessment for operating flights without flight attendants and ensure that an equivalent level of safety is maintained for passengers on the aircraft.
2. Flight crew members assigned to flights must be trained in operations without flight attendants.
3. Aircraft operators must consider the characteristics and capabilities of passengers on the flight, including the level of knowledge of the aircraft type and procedures under normal, abnormal and emergency conditions.
4. The exploitation process must include the following contents:
a) Communication and coordination between crew and passengers;
b) Handling cases where flight crew members are unable to perform their duties;
c) Monitor the passenger compartment;
d) Organize quick escape from the aircraft in case of necessity;
d) Operate and use emergency exits and emergency escape aids;
e) Location and use of oxygen equipment;
g) Location and use of life jackets;
h) Arrange passenger seating to ensure easy access to emergency exits, maintain timely communication with the flight crew and ensure the mass and balance limits of the aircraft;
i) Safety instructions for passengers, including information on the location and use of equipment not shown in the aircraft operator's safety instructions, such as fire extinguishers, first aid equipment (first aid kit, defibrillator), smoke masks and other equipment;
k) Other additional safety instructions when necessary to ensure passenger safety."},"792":{"id":"792","code":"Điều 792","title":"Điều 792. Tiếp viên hàng không tại vị trí làm việc","chapter":"Chương I - TIẾP VIÊN HÀNG KHÔNG","partTitle":"Phần XIII - AN TOÀN KHOANG KHÁCH","partId":"main_part_13","plainText":"Điều 792. Tiếp viên hàng không tại vị trí làm việc
1. Khi tàu bay đang lăn, tiếp viên hàng không phải ngồi tại vị trí làm việc với đai an toàn và dây đeo vai được thắt chặt trừ trường hợp thực hiện công việc liên quan đến sự an toàn của tàu bay và người trên tàu bay.
2. Khi tàu bay cất cánh và hạ cánh, tiếp viên hàng không phải ngồi tại vị trí làm việc với đai an toàn và dây đeo vai thắt chặt.
3. Trong giai đoạn bay bằng, khi có lệnh của người chỉ huy tàu bay, tiếp viên hàng không phải ngồi tại vị trí làm việc với dây an toàn và dây quàng vai thắt chặt.
