Article 792. Flight attendants at work positions
1. When the aircraft is taxiing, flight attendants must sit at their working positions with their seat belts and shoulder straps fastened unless performing work related to the safety of the aircraft and people on board.
2. When the aircraft takes off and lands, flight attendants must sit at their working positions with their seat belts and shoulder straps tightened.
3. During the flight phase, when ordered by the aircraft commander, flight attendants must sit at their working positions with seat belts and shoulder straps tightened.
4. During takeoff and landing, aircraft operators must ensure that flight attendants are positioned as close as possible to the required floor level emergency exits and are distributed evenly throughout the entire passenger compartment to ensure the most effective escape for passengers in case of emergency escape.
5. When passengers are on a parked aircraft, in case the minimum number of flight attendants is reduced, the flight attendant must be in a position consistent with the provisions in the aircraft operator's operating manual to provide the most effective assistance in the event of an emergency escape.
