Article 793. Chief flight attendant
1. When there is a need for more than one flight attendant, the aircraft operator must appoint a chief flight attendant as part of the flight attendant team. The aircraft operator may only appoint a flight attendant to assume the title of chief flight attendant if they fully meet the experience and training requirements as prescribed in Part XIV of these Regulations.
2. The chief flight attendant is responsible to the aircraft commander for the operation and coordination of normal and emergency procedures specified in the operations manual, including stopping non-safety related tasks to ensure safety or security.
3. Aircraft operators must establish a process for selecting the most suitable flight attendant to assume the role of chief flight attendant in case the initially designated chief flight attendant is unable to perform his duties.
4. In case the level of air turbulence is required and when there is no request from the flight crew, the chief flight attendant has the right to decide to suspend non-safety related tasks and notify the flight crew about the level of turbulence occurring and request to turn on the seat belt sign, then proceed to ensure the safety of the passenger compartment and related areas according to regulations."},"translatedText":"Article 793. Chief flight attendant

Article 793. Chief flight attendant
1. When there is a need for more than one flight attendant, the aircraft operator must appoint a chief flight attendant as part of the flight attendant team. The aircraft operator may only appoint a flight attendant to assume the title of chief flight attendant if they fully meet the experience and training requirements as prescribed in Part XIV of these Regulations.
2. The chief flight attendant is responsible to the aircraft commander for the operation and coordination of normal and emergency procedures specified in the operations manual, including stopping non-safety related tasks to ensure safety or security.
3. Aircraft operators must establish a process for selecting the most suitable flight attendant to assume the role of chief flight attendant in case the initially designated chief flight attendant is unable to perform his duties.
4. In case the level of air turbulence is required and when there is no request from the flight crew, the chief flight attendant has the right to decide to suspend non-safety related tasks and notify the flight crew about the level of turbulence occurring and request to turn on the seat belt sign, then proceed to ensure the safety of the passenger compartment and related areas according to regulations."},"794":{"id":"794","code":"Điều 794","title":"Điều 794. Thay thế tiếp viên trưởng không thể thực hiện nhiệm vụ","chapter":"Chương I - TIẾP VIÊN HÀNG KHÔNG","partTitle":"Phần XIII - AN TOÀN KHOANG KHÁCH","partId":"main_part_13","plainText":"Điều 794. Thay thế tiếp viên trưởng không thể thực hiện nhiệm vụ
1. Tiếp viên trưởng không báo cáo hoặc không thể bắt đầu chuyến bay được phân công từ căn cứ của người khai thác phải được thay thế ngay lập tức. Chuyến bay không được phép khởi hành nếu chưa có tiếp viên trưởng khác được chỉ định.
