Article 794. Replacement of chief flight attendant who cannot perform duties
1. Chief flight attendants who do not report to or cannot begin their assigned flight from the operator's base must be replaced immediately. Flights are not allowed to depart unless another chief flight attendant has been assigned.
2. In case of replacing the chief flight attendant who is unable to work or cannot present
a) A chief flight attendant who loses the ability to work during the flight or cannot report to an accommodation location outside the main base must be immediately replaced by another qualified chief flight attendant on the relevant aircraft type. If there is no other chief flight attendant, the most suitable flight attendant must be assigned to take on the role of temporary chief flight attendant to return the aircraft to the operator's base.
b) In the case of a flight sequence with aircraft transiting through the operator's base, the flight attendant currently serving as the temporary chief flight attendant must be replaced by another chief flight attendant at the base.
3. The selection of the most suitable flight attendant to take on the role of temporary chief flight attendant must be based on the level of that individual's operational experience, ensuring sufficient capacity to perform the duties and responsibilities of a chief flight attendant.
4. Selected flight attendants must have practical experience operating on the type or variant of aircraft expected to operate.
5. Aircraft operators specify selection criteria in the operating manual to ensure the designation is consistent with operational safety requirements."},"translatedText":"Article 794. Replacement of chief flight attendant who cannot perform duties

