b) Nghỉ việc do mang thai, nghỉ thai sản, nghỉ chăm sóc con;
c) Nghỉ phép, nghỉ ốm, nghỉ bệnh;
d) Các trường hợp nghỉ việc hợp pháp khác theo quy định của pháp luật lao động.</p>","translations":{"en":"Article 798. Unforeseen situations

Article 798. Unforeseen situations
1. Unforeseen situations are cases related to the loss of the ability to work or the inability to show up for duty by the chief flight attendant or flight attendant.
2. Incapacity for work is a sudden deterioration in health that occurs during flight duty, including during a flight or during the transfer of flights within the same flight duty period outside the operator's base, resulting in the chief flight attendant or flight attendant being unable to perform assigned duties.
3. Inability to work occurring before the aircraft departs from the operator's base is not a basis for reducing the number of flight attendants below the prescribed minimum level.
4. Unable to report for duty: are unforeseen situations at an accommodation location other than the main base that prevent the chief flight attendant or flight attendant from being present to begin the flight duty period, including the following cases:
a) Traffic congestion leads to not being able to arrive on time at the flight crew pick-up point;
b) Difficulties arise with local authorities;
c) Health problems;
d) In case of death;
d) Other objective situations of similar nature.
5. The cases specified in Clause 3 of this Article do not include:
a) Shortage or failure to arrange enough reserve flight attendants;
b) Leave due to pregnancy, maternity leave, child care leave;
c) Leave, sick leave, sick leave;
d) Other cases of legal leave according to the provisions of labor law."},"translatedText":"Article 798. Unforeseen situations

