Article 811. Use of supplemental oxygen
The commander of the aircraft must ensure that he and the flight crew members performing duties essential to the safe operation of the aircraft during the flight must use supplemental oxygen continuously in the following cases:
1. When the pressure altitude in the aircraft cabin exceeds 10,000 ft for more than 30 minutes;
2. When the pressure altitude in the aircraft cabin exceeds 13,000 ft.
Section 2
