Article 840. Requirements for training and inspection programs
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that training, inspection and assessment activities are carried out in accordance with the training program in the operating manual and comply with the regulations in this Part.
2. The training program of aircraft operators complies with the following requirements:
a) In accordance with the provisions of law on civil aviation related to the functions, tasks, responsibilities of each job position and relevant provisions of law;
b) In accordance with the system of documents, policies, regulations, procedures and instructions of the aircraft operator related to each job position;
c) Standards, guidelines and recommendations of the aircraft design country, aircraft manufacturer, aircraft engine and equipment manufacturer or technical documents issued by the design organization.
3. The training program for aircraft operators includes the following contents:
a) Training and testing procedures;
b) Detailed content, duration, completion standards;
c) Forms and methods of training and testing and regulations on separating training activities from testing activities;
d) Personnel performing training, testing and competency standards for each position;
d) Policies and procedures for using training equipment;
e) Process for evaluating effectiveness, reviewing, updating and amending training programs when there are changes in legal regulations, technical standards, aircraft types, forms of operation or results of monitoring operational safety.
4. The training curriculum must be developed in accordance with each training course specified in this Part and must specify in detail the teaching content, training methods, materials used, duration, evaluation standards and implementation methods.
5. When developing a training program for aviation employees, aircraft operators evaluate and recognize completed training content, operational experience or experience in the previous working environment to determine the content to be recognized and the training content that needs to be supplemented, based on the following factors:
a) The compatibility between the completed training content and the aircraft operator's training program;
b) Degree of similarity in aircraft type, operating area, type of operation and operating method;
c) The degree of similarity of the system of legal regulations and operational standards in the environment in which aviation employees work.
6. Validity period of current experience evaluation, training and periodic testing
a) In case the assessment of current experience, training and periodic inspection is completed in the month of expiration or within the last 03 months before the expiration of the validity period, the new validity period is calculated from the original validity expiration date;
b) In case the evaluation of current experience, training or testing is completed before the last 3 months of the validity period, the new validity period is calculated from the last day of the month in which the training or testing is completed."},"translatedText":"Article 840. Requirements for training and inspection programs

