Article 849. Initial training for new aircraft operators and cases of adding new aircraft types
For aircraft operators applying for an aircraft operator certificate for the first time or aircraft operators applying for a new aircraft type:
1. The initial training program for those directly involved in the process of building the documentation system is exempt from the initial training content on the documentation system and procedures of aircraft operators;
2. For the team of aircraft pilots who have experience on the aircraft operator's type of aircraft and participate in the process of building the standard operating procedure documentation system of the aircraft operator, they are allowed to fly under supervision in the simulated cockpit;
3. The teacher conducts flight supervision for aircraft pilots designated by the aircraft operator and meets the following requirements:
a) Participate in developing and understanding the document system and standard operating procedures for new aircraft types;
b) As a flight instructor, a type rating for a new aircraft type is not required at the time of the aircraft operator's initial training;
c) Has conducted training or participated in operations on all routes, airports, operating areas of aircraft operators and performed observation flights during flights under supervision."},"translatedText":"Article 849. Initial training for new aircraft operators and cases of adding new aircraft types

Article 849. Initial training for new aircraft operators and cases of adding new aircraft types
For aircraft operators applying for an aircraft operator certificate for the first time or aircraft operators applying for a new aircraft type:
1. The initial training program for those directly involved in the process of building the documentation system is exempt from the initial training content on the documentation system and procedures of aircraft operators;
2. For the team of aircraft pilots who have experience on the aircraft operator's type of aircraft and participate in the process of building the standard operating procedure documentation system of the aircraft operator, they are allowed to fly under supervision in the simulated cockpit;
3. The teacher conducts flight supervision for aircraft pilots designated by the aircraft operator and meets the following requirements:
a) Participate in developing and understanding the document system and standard operating procedures for new aircraft types;
b) As a flight instructor, a type rating for a new aircraft type is not required at the time of the aircraft operator's initial training;
c) Has conducted training or participated in operations on all routes, airports, operating areas of aircraft operators and performed observation flights during flights under supervision."},"850":{"id":"850","code":"Điều 850","title":"Điều 850. Công nhận nội dung huấn luyện","chapter":"Chương I - QUY ĐỊNH CHUNG","partTitle":"Phần XIV - YÊU CẦU VỀ TRÌNH ĐỘ ĐỐI VỚI NHÂN VIÊN HÀNG KHÔNG CỦA NGƯỜI KHAI THÁC CÓ GIẤY CHỨNG NHẬN NGƯỜI KHAI THÁC TÀU BAY","partId":"main_part_14","plainText":"Điều 850. Công nhận nội dung huấn luyện
