Article 850. Recognition of training content
1. The Vietnam Aviation Administration considers recognizing the experience and existing training records of aviation staff to partially reduce the content or training duration when recognition does not reduce competency standards, inspection requirements and operational safety levels.
2. Recognition is done on the basis of training records, operational experience, similarity in aircraft type, type of operation, operating area, system of procedures and assessment results of aircraft operators.
3. Recognized content, additional training content, inspection and evaluation methods and record keeping responsibilities are specified in the training program or documentation system of the aircraft operator.
