Article 851. Aircraft operator conversion training program for aircraft pilots
1. Aircraft operator conversion training is carried out in the following order:
a) Ground training;
b) Training in the use of emergency and safety equipment before conducting flight training on the aircraft;
c) Flight training and testing on aircraft or simulated flight training equipment.
2. Ground training includes the following contents:
a) Training on specific operating procedures for aircraft operators;
b) Initial ground training on aircraft type;
c) Aviation security training;
d) Dangerous goods training;
d) Safety management system training;
e) Fatigue management training
g) Training in flight crew resource management;
h) Abnormal and emergency procedures, including cases where the driver is incapacitated.
3. Training in the use of emergency and safety equipment is carried out in coordination with flight attendants or other flight crew members when applicable, ensuring coordination and communication procedures between the cockpit and passenger cabin, including the following contents:
a) Initial first aid in the conversion training course of aircraft operators; In case the flight crew member has never completed the initial first aid training content in the aircraft operator's conversion training program, the flight crew member must complete this content before performing the mission;
b) Aviation medicine, including hypoxia, hyperventilation, contamination by fuel or fluids, hygiene, food poisoning and malaria;
c) Effects of smoke and use of equipment in smoky environments;
d) Fire fighting practice;
d) Procedures for coordination with security, rescue and emergency forces;
e) Knowledge and survival skills appropriate to the mining area;
g) Water landing procedures and use of life-saving equipment when appropriate to the type of aircraft, operating area, type of operation or flight crew composition;
h) Location and use of emergency equipment and procedures for handling emergency situations, including emergency exit for passengers;
i) Passenger management in case of operations without flight attendants;
k) Discipline and responsibility in case of operations without assigning flight attendants;
l) Safety instructions for passengers in case of operations without flight attendants;
m) Knowledge of the duties, coordination procedures and corresponding actions of the supervising pilot in emergency and safety exercises that require the supervising pilot's action.
4. Flight training and testing on aircraft or simulated flight training equipment includes the following contents:
a) Flight crew members must complete a competency check and check the use of emergency safety equipment corresponding to the new aircraft type before operating under supervision and pass the in-flight operational test to complete the process of converting aircraft operators.
b) For practical flight training entirely on simulated flight training equipment, the operator clearly stipulates in the operating manual the conditions on the time limit for starting flight operations under supervision, the number of takeoffs and landings as prescribed in the appropriate operational data or technical documents issued by the aircraft design organization.
5. Aircraft operator conversion training is combined in the aircraft type or class conversion training course."},"translatedText":"Article 851. Aircraft operator conversion training program for aircraft pilots

