Article 854. Initial ground training for aircraft types
1. Aircraft operators ensure that flight crew members and flight dispatchers complete the initial ground training program on the aircraft type before being assigned to perform tasks.
2. For flight crew members, the initial ground training course includes contents in the operational manual related to features, weight and balance, operational policies, system limits, normal, abnormal and emergency operations procedures for the type of aircraft being operated.
3. For flight attendants, the initial ground training course includes contents in the operating manual related to specific configuration, aircraft equipment, tasks, normal and emergency operations procedures for the type of aircraft being operated.
4. For flight dispatchers, the initial ground training course includes contents in the operations manual related to flight preparation procedures, aircraft features, weight and balance, operation policies, aircraft systems and operating limits for the type of aircraft being operated.
5. Aircraft operators develop a process to evaluate the level of mastery of flight crew members and flight dispatchers regarding operational limits, aircraft systems and procedures for handling normal, abnormal and emergency situations during training."},"translatedText":"Article 854. Initial ground training for aircraft types

