Article 858. Fatigue management training
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring flight crew members complete training on fatigue management before being assigned to perform tasks.
2. The fatigue management training program has a minimum duration of 02 hours, is developed by the aircraft operator and specified in the operating manual, including the following contents:
a) Regulations on flight time, working time and rest time;
b) Basic knowledge about fatigue, including sleep and the effects of circadian rhythm changes;
c) Causes of fatigue, including health conditions leading to fatigue;
d) Effects of fatigue on the ability to perform tasks;
d) Measures to prevent and minimize fatigue;
e) Effects of lifestyle, nutrition, exercise and family life on fatigue;
g) Identify sleep disorders and take appropriate measures;
h) Effects of long-range mining activities or short-range mining activities with high frequency on each individual;
i) Impact of time zone difference in mining activities;
k) Responsibilities of flight crew members to ensure adequate rest and maintain appropriate health status when performing duties."},"translatedText":"Article 858. Fatigue management training

