6. Aircraft operators develop a program to evaluate the flight operation process under supervision and accumulate initial flight experience to monitor, evaluate and confirm the actual operational capacity of the aircraft pilot.
7. For flights carrying out an operational flight program under supervision to upgrade the rank of chief pilot, the flight examiner or flight instructor assumes the role of aircraft commander. The flight examiner or flight instructor may sit in the observation chair after the pilot meets the following requirements:
a) Has performed 02 takeoffs and landings on that type of aircraft;
