h) Quản lý mệt mỏi.</p>","translations":{"en":"Article 865. Resource management training for flight dispatchers

Article 865. Resource management training for flight dispatchers
1. Flight dispatchers complete initial flight dispatch resource management training before performing their duties and periodic flight dispatch resource management training within a cycle of no more than 12 months according to the aircraft operator's training program. Initial training has a minimum duration of 04 hours; Periodic training has a minimum duration of 02 hours.
2. The flight dispatcher resource management training program is built to improve the capacity to coordinate operations, support decision making, identify and manage threats and errors in operations control activities.
3. The content of the flight dispatcher resource management training program includes the following contents:
a) Communicate and coordinate exploitation;
b) Support for exploitation decision making;
c) Manage workload;
d) Awareness of mining situations;
d) Threat and error management;
e) Human factors in flight dispatching activities;
g) Coordinate with flight crew members, air traffic service providers, aircraft maintenance organizations and related units;
h) Fatigue management."},"translatedText":"Article 865. Resource management training for flight dispatchers

Article 865. Resource management training for flight dispatchers
