Article 867. Training program for multi-member aircraft pilot license holders
1. For a multi-crew pilot license holder who does not have commercial operation experience and continues to work at an aircraft operator that has implemented the initial multi-crew pilot training program, the aircraft operator recognizes the training contents completed in the multi-crew aircraft pilot training program, including standard operating procedures applicable to the type of aircraft and corresponding operating environment.
2. Before assigning independent operations, the aircraft operator must ensure that the multi-member aircraft pilot license holder completes the following:
a) Additional training for changes in regulations, operating documents, equipment, operating methods or safety requirements of aircraft operators since the time of completing the multi-member aircraft pilot training program;
b) Training on specific operating procedures for aircraft operators
c) Aviation security training;
d) Dangerous goods training;
d) Safety management system training;
e) Fatigue management training
g) Training in flight crew resource management;
h) Abnormal and emergency procedures, including incapacitation of the driver.
3. The aircraft operator ensures that the multi-member aircraft pilot's license holder completes the test, evaluates the capacity and accumulates initial flight experience according to the aircraft operator's training program.
4. For a multi-member aircraft pilot license holder who has not completed flying to accumulate initial operating experience at the original aircraft operator and transfer to another aircraft operator, the new aircraft operator shall organize an aircraft operator conversion training program, ensuring the following requirements:
a) Recognition of results of completed training contents in the previous multi-member aircraft pilot training program, except for the contents specified in Point b of this Clause;
b) Re-implement phase 3 and phase 4 of the multi-member aircraft pilot training program appropriate to the type of aircraft, operating environment, standard operating procedures, operating policies and document system of new aircraft operators;
c) Complete testing and assessment of capacity and gain initial operational experience according to the training program for new aircraft operators.
5. For a multi-member aircraft pilot license holder who has completed operational flying under supervision, accumulated initial operational experience at the original aircraft operator and transferred to another aircraft operator, the new aircraft operator shall organize an aircraft operator conversion training program, ensuring the following requirements:
a) Recognize the results of completed training contents in the multi-member aircraft pilot training program and acquired operational experience, except for the contents specified in Point b of this Clause;
b) Re-implement phase 3 and phase 4 of the multi-member aircraft pilot training program appropriate to the type of aircraft, operating environment, standard operating procedures, operating policies and document system of new aircraft operators;
c) Complete the contents of training for aircraft operator conversion as prescribed for aircraft pilots converting aircraft operators, except for the content of standard operating procedures that have been integrated in the training program specified in Point b of this Clause;
d) Perform operational flights under supervision according to requirements applicable to aircraft operator conversion training. The number of flight segments or flight hours operated under supervision is not lower than the level prescribed for aircraft pilots changing aircraft operators.
6. Aircraft operators that have a multi-member flight crew training program are allowed to receive and train aircraft pilots specified in Clauses 4 and 5 of this Article.
7. To receive and continue to organize flights to accumulate initial operating experience for aircraft pilots specified in Clause 4 of this Article, new aircraft operators shall carry out the following contents:
a) Evaluate the capabilities of the pilot;
b) Develop a transition training program, including retraining on standard operating procedures for new aircraft operators and determining the number of flight hours and flight routes needed to accumulate initial operating experience."},"translatedText":"Article 867. Training program for multi-member aircraft pilot license holders

