Article 871. Human factors training and flight crew resource management for flight attendants
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring flight attendants complete training courses on human factors and flight crew resource management before being assigned to perform tasks.
2. Aircraft operators develop a periodic evaluation process to ensure flight attendants maintain knowledge of human factors related to safety and effective coordination among flight crew members.
3. The human factors training and flight crew resource management program is developed by the aircraft operator and specified in the operating manual, including the following contents:
a) Human factors in aviation;
b) Human error;
c) Competence of flight attendants;
d) Management of flight crew resources;
d) Threat and error management;
e) Human performance capabilities in relation to the safety management system;
g) Typical situations."},"translatedText":"Article 871. Human factors training and flight crew resource management for flight attendants

