d) Vệ sinh và an toàn thực phẩm;
đ) Khử khuẩn trong khoang hành khách.</p>","translations":{"en":"Article 872. Aviation medical and first aid training for flight attendants

Article 872. Aviation medical and first aid training for flight attendants
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring flight attendants complete aviation medical and first aid training courses before being assigned to perform tasks.
2. Aircraft operators develop a 12-month periodic assessment process to ensure flight attendants maintain the ability to recognize and handle medical situations on aircraft and perform first aid for common conditions during operations.
3. The aviation medical and first aid training program is developed by the aircraft operator and specified in the operating manual, including the following contents:
a) Handling medical situations on aircraft;
b) Identify, prevent and handle risks related to infectious diseases;
c) First aid;
d) Food hygiene and safety;
d) Disinfection in the passenger compartment."},"translatedText":"Article 872. Aviation medical and first aid training for flight attendants

