Article 883. Observation flights for flight dispatchers
1. The aircraft operator ensures that the flight operations dispatcher conducts 02 cockpit observation flights every 12 months on routes with similar characteristics to the route on which that employee is assigned to perform tasks.
2. Observation flights include landing at airports or take-off and landing sites appropriate to the scope of operations that the flight dispatcher is assigned to perform.
