g) Quản lý khối lượng công việc.
Chương IV
HUẤN LUYỆN PHỤC HỒI CỦA NGƯỜI KHAI THÁC TÀU BAY</p>","translations":{"en":"Article 886. Competency test for flight attendants

Article 886. Competency test for flight attendants
1. After completing the prescribed training program, flight attendants must complete a competency test conducted by a flight attendant test teacher or safety supervisor.
2. Flight attendant competency testing is performed directly on appropriate training equipment through simulated situations to evaluate the flight attendant's ability to perform assigned tasks in fully and effectively performing assigned tasks, including the following contents:
a) Ability to perform normal operating procedures and handle abnormal and emergency situations, including procedures for closing and opening aircraft doors in normal mode, opening emergency doors, using emergency equipment at assigned locations and emergency exits;
b) Situations related to passenger cabin safety, dangerous goods, aviation medicine, first aid and other situations consistent with the flight attendant's duties.
3. For simulated emergency exit situations, flight attendants demonstrate the ability to assess the situation, operate the emergency exit, use appropriate emergency commands, assess external conditions, decide to open the door, and deploy the applicable means of escape within no more than 7.5 seconds from receiving the emergency signal from the flight crew.
4. For practice situations of preparing the passenger cabin for emergency landing on water, flight attendants are arranged at specific locations on the aircraft or appropriate training equipment and follow the procedures of the aircraft operator.
5. Competency testing and assessment for flight attendants is carried out through situational simulation exercises to determine the ability to perform tasks according to the following competency framework:
a) Apply policies and procedures;
b) Communication;
c) Team work;
d) Passenger management;
d) Solve problems and make decisions;
e) Situational awareness and information management;
g) Workload management.
