Article 887. Rehabilitation training for aircraft pilots
1. Aircraft operators conduct rehabilitation training for aircraft pilots when the aircraft pilot does not meet the requirements to maintain license validity, rating or current experience requirements.
2. Aircraft operators develop and detail the recovery training program in the operating manual or training program, including the following contents:
a) Classification of subjects applying rehabilitation training;
b) Operational interruption period corresponding to each level of recovery training;
c) Content, form and duration of rehabilitation training;
d) Require training on a flight simulator, training on an aircraft, flying under supervision or flying to gain initial operational experience when applicable;
d) Require inspection and assessment before returning to exploitation;
e) Conditions for confirming eligibility to return to perform mining duties.
3. The aircraft pilot shall carry out the recovery training program as prescribed in Part VII of these Regulations and the requirements for operating flights under supervision shall comply with the provisions of Article 862 of these Regulations when applicable.
4. The rehabilitation training program as prescribed in Part VII of these Regulations is completed when the aircraft pilot meets the competency assessment requirements. The flight operation phase under supervision is completed when the pilot of the aircraft passes the en route operation check requirements."},"translatedText":"Article 887. Rehabilitation training for aircraft pilots

Article 887. Rehabilitation training for aircraft pilots
