Article 896. Instructors train flight dispatchers
Instructors train flight dispatchers to meet the following standards:
1. Have a valid flight instructor license with appropriate ratings.
2. In addition to the training program for flight dispatchers, instructors who train flight dispatchers complete training on policies, procedures, standards and training methods of aircraft operators.
3. Every 12 months, teachers who train flight dispatchers complete a training competency assessment according to the aircraft operator training program conducted by a flight dispatcher examiner or safety supervisor."},"translatedText":"Article 896. Instructors train flight dispatchers

