Article 899. Periodic assessment of training capacity for instructors training flight dispatchers
1. Periodic assessment of training capacity for instructors training flight dispatchers is carried out in a real training environment or a simulated training environment with the participation of students.
2. Criteria for evaluating training practices for instructors training flight dispatchers include the following contents:
No
Body of knowledge and skills
Detailed content
1
Prepare for training
Ability to prepare lesson plans, documents, meteorological data, flight plans and training equipment and tools appropriate to lesson objectives.
2
Communication and interaction skills
Ability to convey professional knowledge about weather, aircraft features, aviation news announcements, regulations and air traffic control methods clearly and accurately; the ability to encourage students to participate, ask questions and solve problems.
3
Apply professional knowledge to real situations
Ability to build flight dispatching scenarios close to actual operations to evaluate students' ability to handle situations.
4
Evaluate and grade students
Ability to accurately identify students' strengths and areas needing improvement; Ability to evaluate aircraft operators' compliance with standard operating procedures and flight dispatch procedures.
