Article 901. Initial training program for flight attendant instructors
1. Aircraft operators develop a training program to ensure that flight attendant trainers complete the initial training program specified in the training program before performing their duties.
2. The initial training program for flight attendant trainers includes theoretical training with a minimum duration of 12 hours on the system of legal documents on civil aviation, the system of operating documents, the system of safety and quality documents, standard operating procedures of aircraft operators, policies, procedures, standards and training methods of aircraft operators.
3. After completing theoretical training, the flight attendant trainer will observe the classroom and teach under the supervision of the flight attendant trainer designated by the aircraft operator, including the following contents:
a) Observe an entire theoretical training course;
b) Observe 02 practical training exercises;
c) Carry out teaching under supervision for 01 theoretical subject and 02 practical training lessons.
4. In case there is no suitable course to observe or teach under supervision, the flight attendant trainer conducts a teaching session simulating the aircraft operator's training program.
5. After completing the initial training program for aircraft operators, the flight attendant trainer completes a competency assessment, including the following contents:
a) Training objectives;
b) Compile lesson plans;
c) Practical instruction, including use of safety equipment and cabin safety procedures."},"translatedText":"Article 901. Initial training program for flight attendant instructors

Article 901. Initial training program for flight attendant instructors
1. Aircraft operators develop a training program to ensure that flight attendant trainers complete the initial training program specified in the training program before performing their duties.
2. The initial training program for flight attendant trainers includes theoretical training with a minimum duration of 12 hours on the system of legal documents on civil aviation, the system of operating documents, the system of safety and quality documents, standard operating procedures of aircraft operators, policies, procedures, standards and training methods of aircraft operators.
3. After completing theoretical training, the flight attendant trainer will observe the classroom and teach under the supervision of the flight attendant trainer designated by the aircraft operator, including the following contents:
a) Observe an entire theoretical training course;
b) Observe 02 practical training exercises;
c) Carry out teaching under supervision for 01 theoretical subject and 02 practical training lessons.
4. In case there is no suitable course to observe or teach under supervision, the flight attendant trainer conducts a teaching session simulating the aircraft operator's training program.
5. After completing the initial training program for aircraft operators, the flight attendant trainer completes a competency assessment, including the following contents:
a) Training objectives;
b) Compile lesson plans;
c) Practical instruction, including use of safety equipment and cabin safety procedures."},"902":{"id":"902","code":"Điều 902","title":"Điều 902. Chương trình huấn luyện định kỳ đối với giáo viên huấn luyện tiếp viên hàng không","chapter":"Chương V - GIÁO VIÊN HUẤN LUYỆN VÀ GIÁO VIÊN KIỂM TRA","partTitle":"Phần XIV - YÊU CẦU VỀ TRÌNH ĐỘ ĐỐI VỚI NHÂN VIÊN HÀNG KHÔNG CỦA NGƯỜI KHAI THÁC CÓ GIẤY CHỨNG NHẬN NGƯỜI KHAI THÁC TÀU BAY","partId":"main_part_14","plainText":"Điều 902. Chương trình huấn luyện định kỳ đối với giáo viên huấn luyện tiếp viên hàng không
