Article 903. Periodic assessment of training capacity for flight attendant trainers
1. Periodic training competency assessment for flight attendant trainers is carried out during actual theoretical teaching sessions or practical training sessions on appropriate training equipment.
2. Criteria for evaluating training practices for flight attendant trainers include the following contents:
Phase
Criteria for assessing capacity
Request
Prepare and consult
Ability to check documents, lesson plans and operating status of training equipment; Ability to disseminate lesson objectives, training sequences and safety rules during practice.
The training environment is fully prepared and safe; Students clearly understand lesson objectives, implementation procedures and safety regulations.
Teaching and practical guidance
Ability to accurately model emergency operations according to standard operating procedures of aircraft operators; ability to maintain focus, manage classroom and group of students; Ability to detect and guide students to correct operational errors promptly.
Information is communicated clearly and accurately; Students are given appropriate, safe and effective practice conditions.
Handle situations and manage flight crew resources
Ability to coordinate simulation scenarios; Ability to evaluate coordination among trainees in normal, abnormal, and emergency situations.
Training scenarios are close to actual exploitation activities; The teacher appropriately controls the pace, complexity and pressure of the situation.
Comment and evaluate the results
Ability to respond clearly to strengths and areas for improvement, based on actual operations and observable evidence; Ability to evaluate fairly and complete training records.
Students clearly understand errors, causes and remedies; Training records are recorded fully, accurately and transparently."},"translatedText":"Article 903. Periodic assessment of training capacity for flight attendant trainers

