Article 906. Initial training program for flight attendant inspection teachers
1. Aircraft operators develop a training program to ensure that instructors checking flight attendants complete the initial training program specified in the operating manual before performing their duties.
2. The initial training program includes a minimum duration of 08 hours, including the following contents:
No
Knowledge/Skills
Content
1
General knowledge
- Training on document systems and current legal documents.
- Standard operating procedures (SOP).
- Safety management system (SMS), identifying hazards from training results.
- Knowledge about aircraft types.
2
Evaluation and scoring skills
- Evidence-based training and testing skills
- How to apply the rating scale.
- Understanding of the evaluation process.
- Skills in observing, recording errors and evaluating students' level of satisfaction.
- Analyze student strengths and weaknesses, including feedback from students.
- Distinguish between objectivity and subjectivity.
- Standardize assessment skills.
3
Human Factors & Flight Crew Resource Management
- Method for evaluating team coordination and communication skills of flight attendants.
4
Operate training equipment
- How to operate training equipment safely.
- Ensure all assessment activities take place in safe conditions.
5
Feedback Skills
(Debriefing Skills)
- How to give constructive feedback for students to self-aware and overcome.
6
Inspection and reporting process
- Record reviews
- Post-assessment reporting"},"translatedText":"Article 906. Initial training program for flight attendant inspection teachers

