Article 909. Main driver upgrade training program
1. The main pilot upgrade training program for aircraft operators applies to the following cases:
a) Co-pilot is upgraded to main pilot on the same type of aircraft, without changing the assigned aircraft type rating;
b) Co-pilot is upgraded to main pilot combined with changing aircraft type.
2. Aircraft pilots participating in the main pilot upgrade training program of aircraft operators must meet the following requirements:
a) Have a valid airline transport pilot's license with the corresponding aircraft type rating issued or recognized by the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam;
b) Meet the standards and procedures for selecting and upgrading chief pilots of aircraft operators;
c) In the case of upgrading the main pilot combined with changing the aircraft type, the pilot completes the training program to change the aircraft type as prescribed in the training program before performing the training to upgrade the main pilot.
3. The main pilot upgrade training program for aircraft complies with the following requirements:
a) The main pilot upgrade training program includes 03 stages: ground training, training on simulator flight training equipment and operational flight under supervision, ending with on-flight operational check;
b) Ground training includes the following contents:
Subjects
Training content
Minimum duration
Responsibilities and obligations of the main driver
Responsibilities and obligations of the main pilot according to the provisions of Vietnamese law on civil aviation; Certificate of aircraft operator and scope of operations; regulations and procedures on aircraft techniques and aircraft operations for main pilots; decision making and risk management in mining; Responsible for managing, commanding and coordinating with flight attendants, flight dispatchers, maintenance staff, ground staff and other related personnel.
08 o'clock
Human factors and flight crew resource management
Individual perception, human error, and human reliability; attitudes, behavior, self-assessment, self-criticism and learning from experience; managing pressure in aircraft operations; fatigue management; situational awareness, information gathering and processing; use and manage aircraft automation systems; problem solving and decision making.
08 o'clock
Aviation security for main pilot
Responsibilities of the main pilot according to Vietnamese law on aviation security; handle illegal interference and disruptive behavior; cockpit security check procedures and cockpit door protection; Handling reports of bombs and suspicious items and searching for bombs on aircraft.
06 o'clock
c) Training on simulated flight training equipment includes the following contents:
Category section
Training content
Manage normal, abnormal and emergency situations
Mining in adverse weather conditions; abnormal and emergency procedures of the aircraft type; diversion flights and alternate airports; mining in metric units; abort takeoff; Post-takeoff engine failure, including engine failure between V1 and V2 and single engine operation; approach and landing under abnormal flight control conditions or impaired flight protection; in-flight fuel management, minimum fuel status and emergency fuel status; manage fire, smoke, and toxic odor situations during flights; reentry procedures with different power levels and reentry altitudes, including landing aborts.
Flight training based on actual operational scenarios
Carry out the flight according to the actual flight route of the aircraft operator; The training scenario is not announced to the flight crew in advance to ensure effective training for surprise and startle effects; Coordination process with flight attendants and air traffic service providers.
Competency assessment ends
Comprehensive assessment of primary driving capabilities according to the applicable competency framework; The test scenario is not announced to the flight crew in advance to ensure effective assessment of unexpected effects; The final test on a simulated flight training device to evaluate completion of the primary pilot upgrade training program is integrated with the type rating test when applicable and is performed by a flight examiner of the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam.
Low visibility operations and zero flight time training where applicable
Procedures for takeoff and landing in limited visibility conditions; circling and visual approach on a flight simulator.
Prevent and restore abnormal posture
Fly hand in normal protection mode and reduced protection mode, including at low altitude and high altitude; management of the flight automation system, including disconnection, reconnection, and failure handling; aircraft energy management; recognize and recover from abnormal aircraft attitudes; recover from torpor.
The number of training exercises on a simulated flight training device is determined by the aircraft operator in the training program, including a minimum of 05 training exercises, excluding training exercises for special forms of operations, air-time training and competency assessment tests.
d) After meeting the requirements of the training phase on the simulator flight training device, the pilot of the aircraft shall perform flight operations under supervision and inspection of operations on the flight path according to the following requirements:
Phase
Request
Fly operations under supervision
The number of flight segments is determined by the aircraft operator in the training program but must not be less than 60 flights under supervision; performed in the left seat position as the main pilot under the supervision of a flight examiner or flight instructor; Perform all duties and responsibilities of the main pilot during flights under supervision.
Checking flight operations at the end of the program
Conducted by flight examiners of the Vietnam Aviation Administration; Comprehensive assessment of capacity according to the capacity framework of aircraft pilots and standards applicable to main pilots of aircraft operators.
4. The main pilot upgrade training program for helicopters complies with the following requirements:
a) The main pilot upgrade training program includes 03 stages: ground training, training on a flight simulator or on an aircraft and operating under supervision, ending with an operational check on the flight line;
b) Ground training includes the following contents:
Subjects
Training content
Minimum duration
Responsibilities and obligations of the main driver
Responsibilities and obligations of the main pilot according to the provisions of Vietnamese law on civil aviation; Certificate of aircraft operator and scope of operations; regulations and procedures on aircraft techniques and aircraft operations for main pilots; decision making and risk management in mining; Responsible for managing, commanding and coordinating with technical staff, ground staff and other relevant personnel.
