Article 911. Qualifications on flight routes and operating areas for aircraft pilots
1. The aircraft operator assigns an aircraft pilot to perform tasks on a flight route or operating area where the aircraft pilot has no experience after the aircraft pilot completes the familiarization training requirement.
2. Content of familiarization with flight routes, operating areas, equipment and airport methods used includes the following contents:
a) Terrain and minimum safe altitude;
b) Seasonal meteorological conditions;
c) Meteorological, communications and air traffic equipment, services and procedures;
d) Search and rescue methods when available;
d) Navigation equipment associated with the area or flight route expected to operate.
3. Flight route and operating area familiarization training is designed to ensure that aircraft pilots are aware of potential risks and threats of the flight route or operating area that affect operations, based on the application of the threat and error management model or risk management model specified in the aircraft operator's operating manual.
4. Training to familiarize yourself with flight routes and operating areas complies with the following requirements:
a) Built on the basis of the aircraft operator's assessment of potential risks and threats of the flight route or operating area;
b) Aircraft pilots complete initial familiarization training before operating on the route or area of ​​first operation;
c) The aircraft pilot completes recovery training when not operating on that route or operating area within 12 months.
5. Training methods and tools to familiarize yourself with flight paths and operating areas include one or more of the following forms:
a) Training on simulated flight training equipment;
b) Computer training;
c) Fly to become familiar with the role of aircraft commander or co-pilot under supervision;
d) Observation flight;
d) Training through image data or virtual reality;
e) Self-study using documents, audio data or other suitable learning media."},"translatedText":"Article 911. Qualifications on flight routes and operating areas for aircraft pilots

