Article 915. Training to upgrade the rank of chief flight attendant
1. The aircraft operator appoints a flight attendant to hold the position of chief flight attendant when he or she meets the following requirements:
a) Have at least 12 months of continuous experience working as a flight attendant;
b) Complete the training course to upgrade the rank of chief flight attendant and meet the competency assessment requirements for chief flight attendants.
2. Aircraft operators develop standards and procedures for upgrading chief flight attendants, training programs, flight familiarization programs, flying under supervision and evaluate the capacity of chief flight attendants in operational manuals or training programs.
3. The training program to upgrade the rank of chief flight attendant has a minimum duration of 56 hours, excluding aviation security training content when this content is implemented according to specific regulations of the law on aviation security, including the following contents:
