Article 916. Difference training and familiarization training for aircraft pilots
1. The aircraft operator shall ensure that the aircraft pilot completes appropriate differentiation training or familiarization training before being assigned to operate an aircraft that is different from the aircraft type, aircraft variant, equipment, system or procedure for which the aircraft pilot has been trained.
2. Differential training includes additional knowledge and practical training on aircraft, flight simulators or appropriate training equipment, carried out in the following cases:
a) For aircraft, when operating another variant of the same type of aircraft or another type of aircraft of the same class of aircraft being operated, if the difference affects systems, equipment, features, procedures or methods of operation;
b) For helicopters, when operating another variant of the same type of helicopter in operation, if the difference affects the system, equipment, features, procedures or methods of operation.
3. Familiarization training includes supplementing knowledge about aircraft, systems, equipment, procedures or methods of operation and is performed when the pilot operates another aircraft of the same type or class of aircraft, in cases where the level of difference does not require practical training on the aircraft, simulated flight training equipment or appropriate training equipment.
4. Aircraft operators determine the content, duration, training methods, testing methods and completion standards for differences training and familiarization training based on the level of differences of the aircraft, systems, equipment, procedures, operating methods, data suitable for operations or technical documents issued by the aircraft design organization.
