7. The restrictions specified in Clause 5 of this Article may be increased by no more than 01 hour including 01 sector with a continuous flight time of over 09 hours and not exceeding 02 sectors.
8. Rest time on flights using rest facilities must be counted as FDP.
9. The minimum rest time at the destination must be at least equal to the previous duty time or not less than 14 hours, whichever is greater.
10. A flight crew member on a transfer duty cannot be transferred to a flight crew member performing a duty on the same flight.
11. Delays in arrival time due to unforeseen circumstances during operations must comply with the following regulations:
a) The aircraft operator must stipulate the delay in arrival time for duty due to unforeseen circumstances in the operating manual;
b) Records of postponements of time to appear on duty must be kept;
c) The procedure for delaying the time to report for duty must specify a notification time for flight crew members to continue to stay at the appropriate accommodation when this procedure is activated; form of notification; minimum and maximum notification period; Avoid announcements during rest periods when possible.
12. In case a flight crew member is notified of a delay in arriving for duty due to unforeseen circumstances during operations, the FDP is calculated as follows:
a) When there is a notice of delay, the maximum FDP is recalculated based on the provisions of clauses c and d of this Article;
b) If the time to receive the mission continues to be changed, the FDP will be calculated from the time 01 hour after receiving the second notification or from the delay time of being present to receive the mission from the initial notification if earlier;
c) When the delay time to receive the task is less than 04 hours, the maximum daily FDP is calculated from the time of showing up to receive the original task and FDP is calculated from the time of showing up to receive the task according to the delay notification;
d) When the delay in receiving the task is 04 hours or more, the maximum FDP is calculated from the time of being requested to be present to receive the original task or from the time of being present to receive the task according to the postponement notice, whichever is lower, and the FDP is calculated from the time of being present to receive the task according to the postponement notice;
d) In case the aircraft operator announces a delay in the time to report for duty by more than 10 hours or more and the flight crew member is not required to continue to be present for duty, this delay of 10 hours or more is counted as rest time."},"translatedText":"Article 924. Regulations on adjustment of flight duty time

