Article 931. Requirements for backup duties
1. When a flight crew member is assigned a backup duty, the FDP is calculated from the time the flight crew arrives to take over the duty.
2. Time spent performing backup tasks is not counted as time spent performing tasks.
3. Aircraft operators must establish a limit on the maximum number of consecutive days of standby duty.
4. To ensure that flight crew members have the opportunity to get a full 8 hours of sleep, aircraft operators must schedule an 8-hour free period for each scheduled day, based on the principle of fatigue management, and during this time the airline is not allowed to contact the flight crew."},"translatedText":"Article 931. Requirements for backup duties

Article 931. Requirements for backup duties
1. When a flight crew member is assigned a backup duty, the FDP is calculated from the time the flight crew arrives to take over the duty.
2. Time spent performing backup tasks is not counted as time spent performing tasks.
3. Aircraft operators must establish a limit on the maximum number of consecutive days of standby duty.
