Article 933. Requirements for rest periods
1. Interrupted flight schedule:
a) In case the flight schedule of a flight crew member at the main base changes from a late-ending duty or night duty to an early-starting duty, the rest time between 02 FDPs must include 01 night at the locality;
b) In case between 02 rest periods, a flight crew member performs a series of 04 or more missions including night missions, early starting missions or late ending missions, the rest time immediately after the end of this series of missions must be increased to a minimum of 60 hours.
2. Time zone difference:
a) A rotation mission is understood as a series of consecutive missions including at least one flight mission and rest period away from the main base; This mission sequence starts from the main base and ends when the flight crew member returns to the main base and takes a rest period. At this time, the aircraft operator is no longer responsible for arranging accommodation for flight crew members;
b) Aircraft operators must consider the effects of turnaround duties on flight crew members and adjust flight schedules if necessary;
c) Where the flight is conducted in an East-West or West-East direction, rest period must include at least 03 nights in local time which must be provided between 02 consecutive "rotation missions".
d) Monitoring of rotation task combinations must be carried out according to the regulations of the aircraft operator's management system.
3. The effect of time zone difference is compensated by rest time as follows:
a) At the main base, if the rotation duty involves a time zone difference of 04 hours or more, the minimum rest time must meet the following regulations:
Maximum time difference between the reference time and the local time where the flight crew member rests during a "rotation mission"
Time from the first FDP arrival time on a "rotation mission" that involves a time zone difference of 4 hours or more from the reference time
