Article 935. Fatigue management training
1. Aircraft operators must ensure:
a) Flight crew members and flight dispatchers are trained in fatigue management;
b) Flight schedulers and managers involved in flight scheduling receive initial training before performing their duties and periodic training no more than once every 12 months on fatigue management.
2. The fatigue management training program must be built into the operating manual and ensure the following contents:
a) Regulations on flight time, flight duty time, duty time and rest time;
b) Basic knowledge about fatigue;
c) Causes of fatigue;
d) Effects of fatigue on the ability to perform tasks;
d) Measures to prevent and minimize fatigue;
e) Influence of lifestyle, nutrition, exercise and family circumstances;
g) Identify sleep disorders and appropriate treatment measures;
h) Effects of long-range flight operations or short-range flight operations;
i) Effects of time zone difference;
k) Individual's responsibility to ensure adequate rest and maintain appropriate health condition to perform duties.
Chapter III
