2. In case the flight crew is increased by 01 additional member, the maximum daily FDP is extended as follows:
a) 15 hours with class B rest facilities;
b) 16 hours with type A rest facilities.
3. In case the flight crew is increased by 2 additional members, the maximum daily FDP is extended as follows:
a) 16 hours with type B rest facilities;
b) 17 hours with type A rest facilities.
4. The minimum in-flight rest time for flight crew members is 01 hour and 30 minutes for each member; For members who control the aircraft during the final landing, the minimum in-flight rest time is 02 hours.
5. Rest facilities on board the aircraft provide isolation by at least one curtain to ensure darkness and minimize noise to allow each crew member to sleep and comply with the following specifications:
a) Class A resting equipment: is a bed or other surface, of sufficient length and width to accommodate an average person, allowing a flat or nearly flat sleeping position. It can recline at least 80° from vertical;
b) Class B rest facilities: are seats in the passenger cabin of an aircraft that are of sufficient length and width to accommodate an average person, can recline at least 45° from vertical, have a seat width of at least 20 inches (50 cm) and have leg and foot rests.
6. In case of additional flight crew members, the FDP after being extended may be increased by 01 hour if the FDP includes a continuous rest period of 02 hours and 30 minutes in flight for each flight crew member who controls the aircraft during the final landing process;
7. Time spent using in-flight rest facilities is counted towards FDP;
8. The minimum rest time when absent from the main base must be at least equal to the previous duty time, or 14 hours, whichever is greater;
9. FDP can be extended up to 02 hours if the aircraft operator applies FRMS."},"translatedText":"Article 938. Flight duty time may be extended

