Article 939. Unforeseen situations in exploitation
1. The aircraft commander applies limitations on flight time, duty time and rest time in case of unforeseen situations at or after the time of arrival for duty as follows:
a) Maximum daily basic FDP is extended to a maximum of 02 hours; In case of additional flight crew, the maximum FDP can be extended up to 03 hours;
b) If after the increase according to Point a of this Clause, it is necessary to continue to increase that FDP after takeoff on the last flight segment, due to unforeseen circumstances, the flight may continue to the intended destination airport or alternate airport;
c) If after the increase according to point a of this clause, it is necessary to further increase that FDP immediately before take-off on the final flight segment, due to unforeseen circumstances, the flight may continue to the intended destination airport or alternate airport if the immediate and speedy transportation of medical personnel, medical supplies or sick or injured people is absolutely essential;
d) The rest period when absent from the main base, following an extended FDP according to points a, b, c of this Clause, may be shortened but must never be less than 10 hours;
d) The aircraft commander must consult with all flight crew members about their level of alertness before deciding on modifications according to points a, b, c, d of this clause.
2. In case the FDP has ended but there is a delay due to airport operational problems or unexpected inspections by competent state agencies (customs, immigration, law enforcement agencies), this delay time is counted in duty time but is not considered an unforeseen situation."},"translatedText":"Article 939. Unforeseen situations in exploitation

Article 939. Unforeseen situations in exploitation
1. The aircraft commander applies limitations on flight time, duty time and rest time in case of unforeseen situations at or after the time of arrival for duty as follows:
a) Maximum daily basic FDP is extended to a maximum of 02 hours; In case of additional flight crew, the maximum FDP can be extended up to 03 hours;
b) If after the increase according to Point a of this Clause, it is necessary to continue to increase that FDP after takeoff on the last flight segment, due to unforeseen circumstances, the flight may continue to the intended destination airport or alternate airport;
c) If after the increase according to point a of this clause, it is necessary to further increase that FDP immediately before take-off on the final flight segment, due to unforeseen circumstances, the flight may continue to the intended destination airport or alternate airport if the immediate and speedy transportation of medical personnel, medical supplies or sick or injured people is absolutely essential;
d) The rest period when absent from the main base, following an extended FDP according to points a, b, c of this Clause, may be shortened but must never be less than 10 hours;
d) The aircraft commander must consult with all flight crew members about their level of alertness before deciding on modifications according to points a, b, c, d of this clause.
2. In case the FDP has ended but there is a delay due to airport operational problems or unexpected inspections by competent state agencies (customs, immigration, law enforcement agencies), this delay time is counted in duty time but is not considered an unforeseen situation."},"940":{"id":"940","code":"Điều 940","title":"Điều 940. Trì hoãn thời điểm có mặt nhận nhiệm vụ trong các tình huống không lường trước được","chapter":"Chương III - QUẢN LÝ MỆT MỎI TRONG VẬN TẢI HÀNG KHÔNG THƯƠNG MẠI BẰNG MÁY BAY - KHAI THÁC KHÔNG THƯỜNG LỆ SỬ DỤNG MÁY BAY CÓ CẤU HÌNH GHẾ KHÁCH TỐI ĐA TỪ 19 GHẾ KHÁCH TRỞ XUỐNG","partTitle":"Phần XV - QUẢN LÝ MỆT MỎI CỦA NGƯỜI KHAI THÁC CÓ GIẤY CHỨNG NHẬN NGƯỜI KHAI THÁC TÀU BAY","partId":"main_part_15","plainText":"Điều 940. Trì hoãn thời điểm có mặt nhận nhiệm vụ trong các tình huống không lường trước được
