Article 945. Preventive duties
1. In case a flight crew member performs FDP during standby duty, the FDP is calculated from the time he shows up for duty.
2. Standby duty time is not counted as duty time.
3. The number of consecutive days of standby duty must be within the limits.
4. Aircraft operators must schedule eight hours, taking into account fatigue risk management principles, for each day of standby duty during which crew members are not contacted.
5. The minimum notice period for any assignment is 10 hours.
6. Standby duty time does not count as periodic extended rest time."},"translatedText":"Article 945. Preventive duties

