Article 952. Time to perform other tasks
1. In case a flight crew member is assigned to perform tasks on a simulator for testing, training or as an instructor, and during the same time on duty continues to perform duties on the flight, the entire time spent performing tasks on the simulator is fully counted in the flight duty time and duty time. The maximum limit of flight duty time is determined from the moment the flight crew member reports to perform duties on the simulator.
2. A flight crew member may perform flight duties as a member of a single-pilot flight crew until the time the total number of flight hours and duty hours reaches the prescribed limit for a single-pilot flight crew. Thereafter, the flight crew member may extend the flight duty time when additional flight crew members are available and the flight crew must comply with the limits on total flight hours and duty hours for multi-pilot flight crews. During the extended period of flight duty, a flight crew member may not be the commander of the aircraft.
