Article 954. Fatigue risk management system policy
1. FRMS must be set up as follows:
a) The aircraft operator must provide a policy for the FRMS and all components of the system must be clearly identified.
b) The policy must require that the scope and purpose of the FRMS be clearly described in the operations manual.
2. The policy must reflect the sharing of responsibilities among management levels, flight crew members, flight attendants and other relevant individuals;
3. The policy must clearly express the safety objectives of the FRMS;
4. The policy must be approved by the aircraft operator's chief executive officer;
5. The policy must be disseminated with authentic records to relevant departments and management levels of the organization;
6. The policy must demonstrate management's commitment to the effectiveness of safety reporting;
7. The policy must demonstrate management's commitment to ensuring adequate resources for the operation of this system;
8. The policy must demonstrate management's commitment to continuous improvement of the FRMS;
9. The policy must clearly stipulate the responsibilities of management levels, flight crew members, flight attendants and related individuals;
10. The policy must be periodically reviewed to ensure that the FRMS remains consistent and relevant to the operations of aircraft operators."},"translatedText":"Article 954. Fatigue risk management system policy

