KIỂM SOÁT KHAI THÁC</p>","translations":{"en":"Article 958. FRMS promotion process

Article 958. FRMS promotion process
1. The FRMS driven process supports continuous improvement of overall system performance and achievement of optimal safety levels;
2. Aircraft operators must establish and enforce the following as part of the FRMS:
a) Training program to ensure the competence of management levels, flight crew members and relevant individuals in accordance with their roles and responsibilities specified in the FRMS;
b) An effective FRMS communications plan that explains the policies, procedures and responsibilities within the FRMS to relevant individuals and organizations and describes the communication channels used to collect and disseminate FRMS-related information.
