Article 965. Duty time and rest time of flight dispatchers
1. Working hours:
a) In addition to working hours, the aircraft operator can agree with the flight operations dispatcher to work overtime to perform tasks required by aviation operations during both day and night, weekly rest days and holidays, but must ensure the principle: the total number of working hours and overtime hours of the flight operations dispatcher does not exceed 12 hours/day, 232 hours/month; Total overtime hours must not exceed 300 hours in a year.
b) Aircraft operators have the right to mobilize flight dispatchers to work immediately without being limited by the number of working hours or overtime hours per day, in emergency cases that threaten life, security, aviation safety as well as aviation assets and equipment.
2. Rest time:
a) The minimum number of rest hours for flight dispatchers is 12 hours in 24 consecutive hours;
b) Aircraft operators must arrange for flight dispatchers to take enough days off every week, holidays, and New Year; In special cases where weekly breaks are not possible due to the working cycle, the aircraft operator must ensure that flight dispatchers have an average of at least 4 days off per month;
c) If a flight dispatcher works on weekly days off, holidays, or New Year, the aircraft operator must arrange enough days off to compensate;
d) Rest and personal time off shall comply with the provisions of the Labor Code.
