Article 976. Flight dispatch orders when using weather radar
For passenger aircraft flying under instrument flight rules or visual flight rules at night, when meteorological information shows that there are thunderstorms or adverse weather phenomena that can be detected by weather radar, a flight dispatch order will only be issued when the weather radar system is operating normally.
