a) Is of a quality that complies with the packaging instructions of the ICAO Technical Instructions Document (Doc 9284). The packaging must be so constructed and tightly sealed as to prevent any leakage which may occur under normal conditions of transport due to vibration, changes in temperature, humidity or pressure;
b) Suitable for the characteristics of the dangerous goods contained inside. The packaging in direct contact with dangerous goods must be able to withstand chemical reactions or other impacts caused by such dangerous goods;
c) Meets technical standards for materials and structure specified in ICAO's Technical Guidance Document (Doc 9284);
d) Tested according to the provisions of ICAO Technical Guidance Document (Doc 9284).
3. For packaging with the function of holding liquid, it must be able to withstand pressure levels without leaking. Liquid containers must not be filled to the maximum capacity and must leave a safe space as specified in the Technical Instructions Document (Doc 9284) of ICAO.
4. The inner packaging must be lined, secured or padded to prevent breakage, leakage and control movement within the outer packaging under normal air transport conditions. Cushioning materials and waterproofing agents must not react dangerously with the goods contained in the packaging.
5. Do not reuse the packaging until it has been inspected and confirmed to be free of corrosion or other damage. In case of reuse of packaging, all necessary measures must be taken to prevent cross-contamination of the goods contained in the next time.
