4. Separation of packages containing dangerous goods when stored must comply with the following regulations:
a) Do not stack next to each other or in a position that can lead to mutual interaction in case of leakage of packages containing dangerous goods that can react dangerously with each other;
b) Packages containing toxic and infectious substances must be stowed on the aircraft in accordance with the provisions of the Technical Instructions.
5. Packages containing radioactive substances are loaded onto aircraft in compliance with the provisions of the Technical Guidance Document and Vietnamese legal regulations on atomic energy. Packages containing radioactive materials must be stowed on the aircraft to ensure an isolation distance from people, live animals and undeveloped film rolls, and must be secured during the flight according to the provisions of the Technical Instructions."},"1015":{"id":"1015","code":"Điều 1015","title":"Điều 1015. Lưu trữ hồ sơ","chapter":"Chương I - PHÊ CHUẨN VẬN CHUYỂN HÀNG HÓA NGUY HIỂM","partTitle":"Phần XVIII - VẬN CHUYỂN HÀNG HÓA NGUY HIỂM BẰNG ĐƯỜNG HÀNG KHÔNG CỦA NGƯỜI KHAI THÁC CÓ GIẤY CHỨNG NHẬN NGƯỜI KHAI THÁC TÀU BAY","partId":"main_part_18","plainText":"Điều 1015. Lưu trữ hồ sơ
