Article 1022. Reporting incidents and accidents with dangerous goods
1. In the event of an incident, incident or accident involving dangerous goods, the commander of the aircraft and the aircraft operator of the aircraft transporting dangerous goods must immediately comply with the following reporting requirements:
a) Notify the competent authority of the country where the incident occurs regarding dangerous goods transported on the aircraft;
b) Provide information to limit the hazards created by dangerous goods being transported to emergency response units;
c) Notify the Vietnam Aviation Administration.
2. List of incidents, incidents and accidents that must be reported:
a) Dangerous goods are not declared;
b) Dangerous goods are incorrectly declared;
c) Errors during storage and loading;
d) Errors in stacking and separation;
d) Damage and leakage leading to contamination;
e) Dangerous goods are brought onto the aircraft without notifying the aircraft commander;
g) Any dangerous goods incident occurring during flight;
h) Actions to correct the problem or incident have been taken.
