Article 1026. Transport of dangerous goods in specialized aviation
1. Aircraft operators performing specialized flight operations do not require approval to transport dangerous goods when only transporting dangerous goods directly serving specialized operations.
2. Aircraft operators must develop and maintain procedures for managing the transportation of dangerous goods specified in Clause 1 of this Article in the operating manual, including:
a) List of dangerous goods allowed to be transported;
b) Procedures for receiving, preserving, loading, lashing, separating and unloading dangerous goods;
c) Measures to ensure safety and handle emergency situations when incidents related to dangerous goods occur;
d) Procedures for informing flight crew members about dangerous goods being transported.
3. Aircraft operators must ensure that employees performing tasks related to the transportation of dangerous goods are trained on dangerous goods.
