Article 1031. Responsibilities of designated postal operators
Postal operators designated to participate in the provision of international postal services that transport dangerous goods by air are responsible for:
1. Ensure work related to the transportation of dangerous goods by air complies with the requirements of ICAO Technical Instructions (Doc 9284).
2. Develop, promulgate and update training programs and dangerous goods control procedures in accordance with ICAO Technical Guidance Document (Doc 9284). These documents must be sent to the Vietnam Aviation Administration to serve inspection and supervision.
