Article 1036. General requirements
1. Before performing performance-based navigation operations, aircraft operators are responsible for developing, promulgating, implementing and maintaining the following contents:
a) The ability of the aircraft and navigation system to meet each applicable navigation standard;
b) Normal mining process;
c) Abnormal exploitation procedures and contingency procedures;
d) Maintenance procedures to maintain the ability to meet navigation standards;
d) Training and testing program for flight crew members;
e) Training content for flight dispatchers, maintenance personnel and related personnel;
g) Navigation database management process when operations require the use of navigation database;
h) Process for monitoring, reporting and analyzing events related to feature-based navigation operations.
2. Operational guidance documents must clearly define the scope of application for each navigation standard, including aircraft type, aircraft configuration, navigation system, navigation signal source, system functions, airspace, flight path, method, flight phase, operational limits and backup plans.
3. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that operational manuals define the responsibilities of flight crew members, flight dispatchers, maintenance personnel and related personnel in preparing, implementing, monitoring, reporting and handling abnormalities for navigation operations based on performance.
4. Performance-based navigation operations are not performed when the aircraft, navigation system, navigation database, flight crew members, flight dispatchers, operations procedures, maintenance procedures or backup plans do not meet applicable navigation standards.
5. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that changes related to the aircraft, navigation system, software, navigation database, operating manuals, operating procedures, training programs, inspection programs or maintenance programs are managed before continuing to perform the affected operations."},"translatedText":"Article 1036. General requirements

