Article 1037. Requirements for navigation systems and maintenance of airworthiness
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for determining the ability to meet navigation standards of each aircraft, each navigation system configuration and each applicable navigation standard before performing performance-based navigation operations.
2. Determining the ability to meet navigation standards must be based on flight manuals or technical documents issued by the organization responsible for designing the aircraft type, actual system configuration, navigation signal source, display function, warning function, minimum equipment list and conditions for maintaining system capacity.
3. In case the flight manual does not fully demonstrate the ability to meet navigation standards, the aircraft operator is responsible for using the technical documents issued by the organization responsible for designing the aircraft type, the change design organization or the system installation organization to determine the aircraft's meeting capacity.
4. The minimum equipment list must specify equipment, system functions, navigation signal sources, failure conditions and operating limits related to applicable navigation standards.
5. In case the aircraft's response capacity depends on the system configuration, software version, revised standards, installed equipment, navigation signal source or navigation data source, the aircraft operator is responsible for controlling these conditions in the operating manual, maintenance program and minimum equipment list.
6. Individual equipment cannot be used as the sole basis for determining the ability to meet navigation standards when that ability depends on the installation, integration, display, warning or interaction with other aircraft systems.
7. The maintenance program must specify the maintenance, testing, software updates, configuration control and troubleshooting of related systems and equipment to maintain the ability to meet applicable navigation standards.
8. Aircraft may not perform navigation operations based on performance when the system, equipment, function, navigation signal source or navigation data source required according to applicable navigation standards is not operational, except in the case of the minimum equipment list allowing operations with corresponding conditions and limitations."},"translatedText":"Article 1037. Requirements for navigation systems and maintenance of airworthiness

