8. Sai lệch dữ liệu, lỗi dữ liệu, dữ liệu bị thiếu hoặc sự không phù hợp của dữ liệu dẫn đường phải được báo cáo, phân tích nguyên nhân và thực hiện biện pháp khắc phục trước khi tiếp tục sử dụng dữ liệu liên quan cho hoạt động khai thác dẫn đường theo tính năng.</p>","translations":{"en":"Article 1044. Requirements for navigation database

Article 1044. Requirements for navigation database
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that the navigation database used for feature-based navigation operations has appropriate origins, is valid and is suitable for the operating area.
2. The navigation database management process must regulate the reception, inspection, distribution, loading, confirmation, use and handling of data errors according to the aviation data update cycle.
3. The navigation database must include data necessary for the applicable navigation standard, including route, route point, navigation equipment, standard instrument departure procedure, standard instrument arrival procedure, instrument approach procedure, transition points, altitude limits, speed limits, RNP values, transition patterns between flight segments, and procedure segment data when applicable.
4. For instrument flight procedures loaded from the navigation database, the aircraft operator is responsible for ensuring that flight crew members check the procedure name, takeoff and landing routes, transition points, sequence of route points, transition types between flight segments, altitude limits, speed limits, RNP values ​​when applicable and the route displayed on the aircraft system.
5. For RNP APCH, RNP AR APCH, RNP AR DP, RNP 0.3 for helicopters and procedures requiring RF flight functionality, the procedure must be loaded from a valid navigation database, consistent with the published procedure, and not altered in a way that distorts the coded flight path.
6. Flight crew members may not manually enter waypoint coordinates, flight paths, altitude limits, speed limits, RNP values, RF flight functions, or procedure segment data when manual entry would change the encoded data in the navigation database.
7. Navigation data shall not be used when it is discovered that expired data, data errors, data errors, missing data or incompatibility between data in the aircraft system and the relevant aeronautical information file, aeronautical information notice or procedure chart.
8. Data discrepancies, data errors, missing data or inadequacies of navigation data must be reported, the cause analyzed and corrective measures taken before continuing to use the relevant data for feature-based navigation operations."},"translatedText":"Article 1044. Requirements for navigation database

