8. Quy trình bất thường và quy trình dự phòng đối với RNP 4 phải bao gồm việc xử lý mất hoặc suy giảm hệ thống dẫn đường tầm xa, cảnh báo không đáp ứng RNP, mất hoặc suy giảm nguồn tín hiệu dẫn đường, sai lệch đường bay vượt giới hạn, sai lệch giữa các hệ thống dẫn đường tầm xa vượt giới hạn, mất liên lạc không lưu hoặc phải bay lệch đường bay trong vùng trời đại dương hoặc vùng trời xa khu vực có hạ tầng dẫn đường mặt đất.</p>","translations":{"en":"Article 1048. Requirements for RNP exploitation 4

Article 1048. Requirements for RNP exploitation 4
1. RNP 4 operations are carried out in oceanic airspace, airspace far from areas with ground navigation infrastructure, flight paths or operating areas announced to apply RNP 4.
2. Aircraft implementing RNP 4 must be equipped with at least two independent, operational long-range navigation systems, suitable to the airspace, flight path, flight time in the area where RNP 4 is applied and the applicable backup plan.
3. The navigation system used for RNP 4 must use the global navigation satellite system as an independent navigation signal source or as a navigation signal source in a multi-sensor system in accordance with the flight manual or technical documents issued by the organization responsible for designing the aircraft type.
4. The navigation system used for RNP 4 must have the function of monitoring and warning the aircraft's navigation features in accordance with the RNP 4 value.
5. Before entering the airspace, flight path or operating area applying RNP 4, flight crew members are responsible for checking and confirming the ability to continue to meet RNP 4, long-range navigation system status, navigation signal source, system warnings, flight path deviations and flight path displayed on the aircraft system.
6. During flight in the airspace, flight path or operational area applying RNP 4, flight crew members are responsible for monitoring flight path deviations, navigation signal source status, navigation performance monitoring and warning functions, RNP non-response warnings and the compatibility between the displayed flight path and the air traffic flight plan or clearance of the air traffic service provider.
7. RNP Operational Procedures 4 must provide for the use of parallel flight paths when this feature is announced, authorized by the air traffic services facility and supported by the aircraft navigation system.
8. Abnormal procedures and contingency procedures for RNP 4 must include handling loss or deterioration of long-range navigation systems, warnings of failure to respond to RNP, loss or deterioration of navigation signal sources, deviations of flight paths beyond limits, deviations between long-range navigation systems beyond limits, loss of air traffic contact or having to fly off-course in oceanic airspace or airspace away from areas with ground navigation infrastructure."},"translatedText":"Article 1048. Requirements for RNP exploitation 4

