11. Trường hợp phương thức bay lại của RNP APCH sử dụng thiết bị dẫn đường thông thường, thiết bị dẫn đường cần thiết phải được lắp đặt, còn hoạt động và được thành viên tổ lái kiểm tra trước khi thực hiện phương thức.
12. Quy trình bất thường và quy trình dự phòng đối với RNP APCH phải bao gồm việc xử lý mất khả năng đáp ứng loại giá trị khai thác dự kiến, cảnh báo không đáp ứng RNP, mất hoặc suy giảm hệ thống vệ tinh dẫn đường toàn cầu, mất hoặc suy giảm hệ thống tăng cường dựa trên vệ tinh khi thực hiện LP hoặc LPV, dẫn đường thẳng đứng khí áp không còn sử dụng được khi thực hiện LNAV/VNAV, sai lệch đường bay vượt giới hạn, dữ liệu đoạn tiếp cận cuối hoặc đường bay thẳng đứng không phù hợp và huấn lệnh của cơ sở cung cấp dịch vụ không lưu không phù hợp.</p>","translations":{"en":"Article 1051. Requirements for RNP APCH exploitation

Article 1051. Requirements for RNP APCH exploitation
1. RNP APCH operations are conducted on published instrument approaches that apply RNP APCH and are not RNP AR APCH.
2. RNP APCH includes the following mining value types:
a) LNAV;
b) LNAV/VNAV;
c) LP;
d) LPV.
3. Aircraft performing RNP APCH must meet applicable navigation standards for instrument approach methods, operational value types, reentry procedures, airports, runways and related operating conditions.
4. Flight manuals or technical documents issued by the organization responsible for designing the aircraft type must demonstrate the aircraft's ability to meet RNP APCH for the applicable operational value type.
5. The navigation system used for RNP APCH must have the function of monitoring and warning on aircraft navigation features appropriate to the approach phase, RNP value and type of applicable operational value.
6. For RNP APCH to LNAV values, the aircraft must be capable of horizontal navigation using the global navigation satellite system and the operating procedures must stipulate the use of minimum descent altitude or minimum descent height.
7. For RNP APCH up to LNAV/VNAV value, the aircraft must be capable of horizontal navigation using a global navigation satellite system and vertical navigation using a barometric vertical navigation system; Operational procedures shall specify the use of decision altitude or decision height, barometric placement, temperature limits, temperature corrections, and conditions for disuse of barometric vertical navigation where applicable.
8. For RNP APCH up to LP value, the aircraft must be capable of horizontal navigation using a satellite-based augmentation system and the operating procedures must specify the use of minimum descent altitude or minimum descent height.
9. For RNP APCH up to LPV values, the aircraft must be capable of horizontal and vertical navigation using a satellite-based augmentation system; Operational procedures must stipulate the use of decision altitude or decision height and the readiness check of the satellite-based augmentation system before executing the procedure.
10. Before performing RNP APCH, the flight crew member is responsible for checking the type of operational value, minimum value, procedure name, runway, transition point, route point sequence, altitude limit, speed limit, RNP value, final approach point, reentry point, displayed flight path and the availability of the navigation signal source in accordance with the type of operational value expected to be used.
11. In the case of an RNP APCH reentry procedure using conventional navigation equipment, the necessary navigation equipment must be installed, operational and inspected by the flight crew member prior to executing the procedure.
12. Abnormal procedures and contingency procedures for RNP APCH should include addressing the loss of ability to meet the expected operational value class, RNP non-response warnings, loss or degradation of the global navigation satellite system, loss or degradation of the satellite-based augmentation system when performing LP or LPV, loss of barometric vertical guidance when performing LNAV/VNAV, off-limit deviations, final approach data or flight paths. inappropriate vertical position and inappropriate clearance from the air traffic service facility."},"translatedText":"Article 1051. Requirements for RNP APCH exploitation

