5. When there are changes related to the aircraft or system, the aircraft operator is responsible for re-determining the aircraft's ability to meet navigation standards on the basis of actual configuration, flight manuals, technical documents, minimum equipment list, maintenance program and applicable operating conditions.
6. When there are changes related to software, system database or system functions, aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that the impact of changes on navigation, display, warning, monitoring of navigation features, RF flight functions, parallel flight path displacement, fixed radius transitions and other related functions are evaluated before use in PBN operations.
7. When there are changes related to the navigation database, the aircraft operator is responsible for ensuring that the new data is received, checked, loaded, confirmed and distributed according to the navigation database management process before use.
8. When changes create new risks or change the level of identified risks, aircraft operators are responsible for updating operational safety assessments and determining appropriate mitigation measures before continuing to carry out related PBN operations.
9. Mitigation measures for changes should be specified in operational manuals, training programs, inspection programs, maintenance programs, minimum equipment lists, navigation database management procedures or operational monitoring procedures as appropriate.
10. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that flight crew members, flight dispatchers, maintenance personnel and related personnel are disseminated or trained on changes, operational limitations, applicable conditions, modification procedures, mitigation measures and contingency plans before performing tasks affected by changes.
11. Information about changes, impact assessment results, mitigation measures, document updates, dissemination or training content and post-change monitoring results must be kept and ready for the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam to check when necessary.
12. Aircraft operators must not continue to operate PBN operations affected by changes when the impact of the change has not been assessed, mitigation measures have not been implemented or relevant personnel have not been properly disseminated or trained.
