Article 1064. Altitude holding error in operations to reduce minimum altitude separation
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for reporting recorded or reported incidents related to altitude holding errors due to aircraft equipment malfunctions or operational factors, when the errors have an absolute value equal to or greater than the following thresholds:
a) Total height error equal to or greater than 90 m (300 ft);
b) Altimeter system error equal to or greater than 75 m (245 ft);
c) Specified elevation deviation equal to or greater than 90 m (300 ft).
2. Incident reports must be sent to the Vietnam Aviation Administration within 72 hours from the time the incident occurs or is discovered.
3. The incident report must include the results of the initial analysis of the cause and measures to prevent recurrence.
4. When recording or receiving notice of altitude holding error, the aircraft operator is responsible for immediately taking measures to correct the cause of the error and providing monitoring reports when requested.
