Article 1066. Requirements for long-range navigation systems
1. For operations in airspace applying MNPS, aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that aircraft are equipped with two independent long-range navigation systems.
2. Long-range navigation system includes one of the following systems:
a) Inertial navigation system;
b) Global navigation satellite system;
c) The navigation system uses input data from one or more inertial reference systems or other sensor systems that meet the requirements of the MNPS.
3. In case the global navigation satellite system is used as an independent long-range navigation system, the aircraft operator is responsible for checking the integrity of the navigation data.
4. For operations in the airspace applying MNPS according to announced specialized airways, aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that the aircraft is equipped with at least one long-range navigation system.
