Article 1070. Procedures for operation and monitoring in the North Atlantic high-flying airspace
1. Before entering the North Atlantic high-flying airspace, the flight crew is responsible for checking the accuracy of long-range navigation systems operating independently at a check point located within a range of not more than 200 NM from the point of entry into the oceanic airspace.
2. Aircraft operators are responsible for establishing monitoring procedures, collecting information and reporting to the Vietnam Aviation Administration of incidents related to navigation errors exceeding 10 NM or altitude errors exceeding 300 ft.
3. In case the monitoring data of the regional supervisory agency determines that the aircraft operator does not maintain the level of operational safety required for operations in the North Atlantic high-flying airspace, the aircraft operator is responsible for stopping the relevant operation, taking corrective measures and only continuing the operation when the applicable safety requirements are met.
