Article 1074. Approach using Class II equipment in conditions of limited visibility
1. For approach operations using type II equipment, aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring the following requirements:
a) The decision altitude is determined by a radio altimeter;
b) The decision altitude is not lower than the value specified in the aircraft's flight manual, if any;
c) The decision altitude is not lower than the obstacle clearance altitude applicable to the aircraft class;
d) The decided altitude is not lower than the altitude at which the flight crew member meets the competency requirements to perform operations;
d) Decision height is not lower than 100 ft;
e) The minimum runway visibility value is not lower than the value specified in Clause 2 of this Article.
