Article 1076. Effects of temporary equipment failure or performance degradation on minimum landing standards
1. For approach operations using type II equipment and approach operations using type III equipment, aircraft operators are responsible for determining the impact of temporary equipment failure or performance degradation on minimum landing standards.
2. Determining the impact of temporary equipment failure or performance degradation on minimum landing standards must meet the following requirements:
a) Does not apply to cases of simultaneous failure of the runway lighting system or the final approach and takeoff area, except for the cases specified in Clause 3 of this Article;
b) In case of simultaneous failure of the approach lighting system and the runway lighting system or the final approach and takeoff area, more stringent operational consequences will apply;
c) For approaches with decision altitudes below 200 ft, deterioration of the runway lighting system or final approach and takeoff area shall not be combined with degradation of the runway visual assessment system;
d) Other failures, other than the instrument landing system, satellite guided landing system or microwave landing system, only affect the runway visibility value and do not affect the decision altitude.
