Article 1079. Operation applies operation credit to the use of enhanced visibility support system when flying to the runway edge
1. When performing operations using the enhanced visibility support system when flying to the runway, the aircraft operator is responsible for ensuring that the decision altitude is not lower than the decision altitude applied to the corresponding operation without using the enhanced visibility support system during flight.
2. The minimum runway visibility value is determined in one of the following ways:
a) According to the criteria specified in the aircraft's flight manual for expected weather conditions;
b) In case the aircraft's flight manual does not specify, it is determined by reducing the value of runway visibility or the converted visibility level applicable to operations that do not use the enhanced vision support system when flying or the combined vision system.
3. The value of runway visibility or converted visibility level for operations using an enhanced vision support system in flight or a combined vision system, compared to the value required when not using this system, is determined as follows:
Runway visibility value or conversion visibility level required when not using enhanced visual aids in flight
The runway visibility value or conversion visibility level when using the enhanced visibility system in flight
