b) Tối thiểu một yếu tố ngang của hệ thống tín hiệu mặt đất, bao gồm dải đèn ngang của hệ thống đèn tiếp cận, thềm đường cất hạ cánh hoặc dải đèn vùng chạm bánh, trừ trường hợp hoạt động khai thác được thực hiện bằng hệ thống hiển thị thông tin trên kính lái đến điểm chạm bánh.</p>","translations":{"en":"Article 1084. Mining procedures for access mining activities using type III equipment

Article 1084. Mining procedures for access mining activities using type III equipment
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that Class III instrument approach operations are carried out with a flight crew consisting of at least two flight crew members.
2. The aircraft operator is responsible for ensuring that the approach method is performed using the system specified in the aircraft's flight manual or documents issued by the organization responsible for designing the aircraft type.
3. Where the approach is performed using an autopilot and a manual landing, the aircraft operator is responsible for ensuring that the autopilot remains connected until the flight crew member identifies and maintains the required visual references.
4. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that altitude commands are below 200 ft above the runway elevation determined by radio altimeter.
5. In case the aircraft flight manual or documents issued by the organization responsible for designing the type of aircraft require it, the aircraft operator is responsible for ensuring that the decision altitude is determined by a radio altimeter.
6. In the case of a decision-altitude Class III instrument approach operation, at the decision altitude, the aircraft operator is responsible for ensuring that the following visual references are clearly displayed and identified by flight crew members:
a) The segment includes at least three consecutive lights, which are center lights of the approach light system, touchdown zone lights, runway center lights, take-off and landing curb lights, or a combination of these lights;
b) At least one horizontal element of the ground signaling system, including the horizontal light strip of the approach lighting system, runway apron or touchdown zone light strip, except where operations are carried out by means of a system that displays information on the windshield up to the touchdown point."},"translatedText":"Article 1084. Mining procedures for access mining activities using type III equipment

