5. At decision altitude, the aircraft operator is responsible for ensuring that the following visual references are clearly displayed and recognized by flight crew members:
a) The segment includes at least three consecutive lights, which are center lights of the approach light system, touchdown zone lights, runway center lights, take-off and landing curb lights, or a combination of these lights;
b) Visual reference includes at least one horizontal element of the ground signaling system such as the horizontal light strip of the approach lighting system, runway apron or touchdown zone light strip."},"translatedText":"Article 1086. Mining process for access mining activities using type II equipment applying mining credits

