Article 1103. Summary method of assessment
1. The abridged evaluation method is applied in the following cases:
a) Aircraft operators intend to start operating EDTO when they have less than 01 year of experience directly operating the type of aircraft expected to operate EDTO;
b) The aircraft operator has direct experience in operating the type of aircraft expected to operate EDTO but is expected to perform EDTO operations exceeding the maximum diversion time of 120 minutes when having less than 01 year of experience operating EDTO with a maximum diversion time of 120 minutes for that type of aircraft.
2. For the abbreviated assessment method, the aircraft operator is responsible for ensuring documents demonstrate the ability to meet EDTO operational requirements for the expected operational scope, including the following contents:
a) Flight manuals, EDTO appendices of flight manuals, certificates of conformity with technical standards or technical documents issued by the organization responsible for designing the type of aircraft showing EDTO capabilities of the aircraft and engine combination, maximum navigation time, limits of critical systems operating EDTO with time limits and related operating limits;
b) EDTO configuration, maintenance and procedure documents applicable to the aircraft and engine combination must identify the minimum configuration of the aircraft, special inspection requirements, hardware life limits, constraints on the original minimum equipment list, EDTO maintenance work and necessary operation and maintenance procedures to perform EDTO operations;
c) EDTO operation process, including planning EDTO flight operations, determining EDTO reserve airports, critical fuel for EDTO operations, checking and confirming before exceeding the threshold time and handling diversions;
d) EDTO maintenance program, EDTO reliability program, control of duplicate maintenance work for EDTO key systems, spare parts control and monitoring of EDTO key systems;
d) EDTO training program for flight crew members, flight operations dispatchers, flight operations control personnel and related maintenance personnel;
e) Methods of monitoring, reporting, storing, evaluating and analyzing exploitation data, technical data and maintenance data after performing EDTO exploitation;
g) Risk control measures during the initial stages of EDTO exploitation or during the period of extending the maximum diversion period.
3. According to the shortened assessment method, the scope of EDTO operations is determined to not exceed 180 minutes of maximum diversion time and can be applied from the time the aircraft type is put into operation when the aircraft operator proves that it fully meets the requirements of the aircraft, engine, configuration, configuration documents, maintenance and EDTO procedures, EDTO maintenance program, EDTO reliability program, EDTO training program, EDTO operation procedures, systems. flight operations regulation and monitoring system after being put into operation."},"translatedText":"Article 1103. Summary method of assessment

