Article 1106. Minimum operating standards for EDTO reserve airport
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that minimum operational standards for the EDTO reserve airport are determined and applied specifically for the flight operation planning stage and the actual use stage of the EDTO reserve airport.
2. When planning EDTO flight operations, the aircraft operator is responsible for ensuring that the EDTO reserve airport designated in the flight operation plan or flight dispatch order meets the minimum operational standards applicable to the EDTO reserve airport from the earliest expected time of landing to the latest expected time of landing at that airport.
3. Minimum operational standards when planning for the EDTO reserve airport are determined on the basis of the approach method expected to be used, navigation equipment, aircraft equipment, crew member capabilities, runway conditions, air traffic services, communications, rescue, firefighting and related airport operating conditions.
4. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that meteorological bulletins, meteorological forecasts and meteorological information related to the EDTO reserve airport are evaluated during the period from the earliest expected time of landing to the latest expected time of landing at that airport.
5. The time period specified in Clause 4 of this Article is determined in the operating manual on the basis of the earliest expected time and the latest expected time the aircraft can land at the EDTO reserve airport.
6. When actually using the EDTO reserve airport, flight crew members are responsible for assessing meteorological conditions, airport conditions, runway conditions, air traffic services, communications, navigation equipment, rescue, firefighting and related operational restrictions at the time of diversion and the expected time of landing.
7. The EDTO alternate airport is used in practice when meteorological and aerodrome conditions meet the minimum operational standards applicable to the approach and landing procedure intended to be used.
8. Aircraft operators are responsible for stipulating in the operating manual the method of determining minimum operational standards for the EDTO reserve airport, the method of evaluating meteorological reports, meteorological forecasts, the applicable time period for the expected time of landing and the assessment responsibilities of flight crew members when actually using the EDTO reserve airport."},"translatedText":"Article 1106. Minimum operating standards for EDTO reserve airport

