Article 1115. Requirements for EDTO training program
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that the initial and periodic EDTO training program is established, maintained and applied to flight crew members, flight operations dispatchers, flight operations control personnel and related maintenance personnel.
2. The EDTO training program for flight crew members includes the following contents:
a) EDTO operating principles, threshold time, maximum diversion time, EDTO operating area and EDTO flight route;
b) Plan EDTO flight operations, identify EDTO reserve airports, EDTO key points and key fuels for EDTO operations;
c) Critical systems for EDTO operations, time-limited critical systems for EDTO operations and the impact of failure or performance deterioration of these systems on EDTO flights;
d) Verification procedures before threshold times are exceeded, monitoring EDTO alternate airfield conditions, monitoring fuel, and determining alternatives;
d) Procedures for redirection, communication, and coordination with air traffic service providers, flight operations dispatchers, and flight operations control personnel;
e) Procedures for handling unusual and emergency situations in case of engine failure, decompression, fire, smoke, loss or deterioration of critical EDTO operating systems and other situations affecting the ability to continue EDTO flights.
3. EDTO training program for flight dispatchers and flight control personnel includes the following contents:
a) Plan EDTO flight operations, determine EDTO flight routes, EDTO reserve airports, diversion times and key fuel for EDTO operations;
b) Evaluate meteorological bulletins, meteorological forecasts, aeronautical information announcements, EDTO reserve airport conditions and related operational restrictions;
c) Monitor EDTO flights, update operating conditions, coordinate with flight crew members and determine alternative plans when operating conditions change;
d) Procedures for coordination, information exchange and support for flight crew members in unusual situations, emergencies or diversions.
4. EDTO training program for relevant maintenance personnel includes the following contents:
a) EDTO maintenance program, EDTO reliability program and EDTO configuration, maintenance and procedure documentation;
b) EDTO maintenance work for engines, auxiliary power equipment, critical systems for EDTO operations, and critical systems for EDTO operations with time limits;
c) Control duplicate maintenance work for the same critical system operating EDTO, control spare parts, technical configuration and applicable content in the minimum equipment list;
d) Monitoring of in-flight engine shutdown, engine condition, oil consumption, ability to start auxiliary power equipment in-flight and technical events related to EDTO;
d) Report, evaluate and handle incidents, failures or technical events that affect EDTO exploitation.
5. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that personnel assigned tasks related to EDTO flights complete EDTO training in accordance with their assigned functions and tasks before performing their duties.
6. The aircraft operator is responsible for specifying in the operating manual or training documents the content of EDTO training, periodic training cycles, training completion standards, evaluation methods and requirements for storing training results."},"translatedText":"Article 1115. Requirements for EDTO training program

