Article 1117. Changes affecting EDTO exploitation activities
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for evaluating any changes that affect EDTO operations before applying the changes.
2. Changes that affect EDTO mining operations include the following cases:
a) Change maximum diversion time;
b) Change the aircraft and engine combination;
c) Changing operating areas, routes or groups of EDTO routes;
d) Change the EDTO reserve airport or the method of selecting, evaluating and designating the EDTO reserve airport;
d) Change the EDTO exploitation process;
e) Changes to the EDTO maintenance program, EDTO reliability program or EDTO configuration, maintenance and procedure documentation;
g) Change EDTO training program;
h) Change the list of minimum equipment, critical systems for EDTO exploitation or time-limited critical systems for EDTO exploitation that affect EDTO exploitation.
3. Before applying the changes specified in Clause 2 of this Article, aircraft operators are responsible for updating documents that meet the requirements for EDTO operations and related documents to demonstrate the ability to meet EDTO operation requirements for EDTO operations expected after the change.
4. Documents specified in Clause 3 of this Article include contents related to the aircraft, engine, maximum diversion time, operation area, flight route, EDTO reserve airport, key fuel for EDTO operation, operation process, maintenance program, reliability program, training program and post-change monitoring method.
5. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that post-change EDTO operations are carried out in accordance with documents that meet the requirements for EDTO operations, maintenance documents, reliability programs, training programs, minimum equipment lists and applicable operating conditions.
6. After applying changes that affect EDTO operations, aircraft operators are responsible for monitoring, storing, evaluating and analyzing relevant operational data, technical data and maintenance data to maintain the ability to meet EDTO operations requirements.
