Article 1119. Requirements before using electronic flight documentation application
1. Aircraft operators using Class B electronic flight documentation applications or electronic flight documentation functions that directly serve safe operations are responsible for ensuring that such applications or functions are evaluated before being used in flight operations.
2. Evaluation includes the following contents:
a) Type of operation, aircraft type, aircraft variant, aircraft fleet or applicable aircraft registration number;
b) Electronic flight documentation equipment, hardware platform, rack, power source, connection to aircraft systems and configuration for use in the cockpit;
c) Type B electronic flight documentation application or electronic flight documentation function used;
d) Phase of the flight, duties of flight crew members and related personnel when using the application or electronic flight documentation function;
d) Forms of using backup paper documents, other electronic backups or paperless operations;
e) Limits of use, operating conditions and solutions when devices, applications, databases, power sources or connections do not work normally.
3. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that operating manuals, training programs, minimum equipment lists, if applicable, operating procedures and electronic flight documentation system management documents are consistent with the assessment results specified in Clause 1 of this Article."},"translatedText":"Article 1119. Requirements before using electronic flight documentation application

Article 1119. Requirements before using electronic flight documentation application
