4. Người khai thác tàu bay có trách nhiệm đánh giá định kỳ hiệu quả của hoạt động quản trị hệ thống tài liệu bay điện tử và thực hiện biện pháp khắc phục khi phát hiện nội dung không phù hợp, lỗi dữ liệu, lỗi phần mềm, hỏng hóc thiết bị hoặc nguy cơ mới đối với an toàn khai thác.</p>","translations":{"en":"Article 1124. Management of electronic flight documentation system

Article 1124. Management of electronic flight documentation system
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for establishing and maintaining the management of the electronic flight documentation system in accordance with the scale, level of complexity and content of the assessed use of electronic flight documents.
2. Electronic flight document management system includes the following contents:
a) Assign an individual or department to be responsible for overall management of the electronic flight documentation system;
b) Manage hardware configuration, operating system, applications, software versions, databases, data sources and connection to aircraft systems;
c) Ensure that only current software, applications, versions and data packages, suitable for assessed usage content, are released and used in exploitation activities;
d) Prevent the installation, modification, deletion, disabling or use of uncontrolled software, applications or data;
d) Manage access rights, user accounts, administrative accounts, backup, restore data, protect against malware and ensure data integrity;
e) Control the responsibilities of software providers, data providers, support service providers and organizations hired to perform work related to electronic flight documents;
g) Manage maintenance, inspection, replacement, charging of batteries, charging equipment, connection accessories, handling of damaged batteries, overheating or equipment damage;
h) Store system configuration, software version, database version, update results, errors, failures, remedies, training, exploitation evaluation and changes.
3. Personnel involved in managing electronic flight documents must be trained in accordance with their assigned responsibilities and have knowledge of equipment configuration, operating system, applications, databases, operating procedures, safety requirements and related usage limitations.
4. Aircraft operators are responsible for periodically evaluating the effectiveness of electronic flight documentation system management activities and taking corrective measures when detecting inappropriate content, data errors, software errors, equipment failures or new risks to operational safety."},"translatedText":"Article 1124. Management of electronic flight documentation system

