Article 1127. Data management, software, security and electronic confirmation
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that data, software, applications and databases used on the Type B electronic flight documentation application or the electronic flight documentation function directly serving safe operations are controlled from source of supply to use in flight operations.
2. Data, software and security management process includes the following contents:
a) Control data sources, procedures for receiving, processing, releasing, loading, checking and confirming data before use in flight operations;
b) Check the currentness, completeness, integrity and traceability of data, software, applications and databases;
c) Manage operating system versions, applications, databases, patches, device configurations and update history;
d) Manage access rights of users, administrators, data providers, software providers and technical support organizations;
d) Protect operating systems, applications, databases and devices from malware, unauthorized access, uncontrolled modification or data loss;
e) Handling incorrect data, expired data, incomplete data, inconsistent data or inaccessible data;
g) Back up, restore and ensure access to data necessary for safe mining operations.
3. In case of using electronic forms, electronic confirmations or electronic signatures on electronic flight documents, the aircraft operator is responsible for ensuring the identification of the person performing the implementation, the time of implementation, the content to be confirmed and the integrity of the data after confirmation.
4. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring data management, software, security and electronic confirmation processes are appropriate to the level of impact on operational safety of each application or electronic flight document function."},"translatedText":"Article 1127. Data management, software, security and electronic confirmation

