Article 1134. Requirements for aircraft and equipment
1. Aircraft used to perform single-pilot aircraft operations under instrument or night flight rules must meet the following requirements:
a) The flight manual does not require a flight crew of more than one person;
b) Is a propeller-driven aircraft;
c) Have a maximum passenger seat configuration of no more than 09 seats;
d) Have a maximum takeoff weight not exceeding 5,700 kg.
2. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that aircraft used for single-pilot operations under instrument or night flight rules are equipped and maintained in normal operating condition with the following equipment:
a) The autopilot system has the function of holding altitude and selecting flight direction;
b) Headphones with microphone or equivalent communication device;
c) Means of displaying aeronautical charts used in flight, ensuring readability in all environmental light conditions;
d) For operations according to instrument flight rules, two independent barometric altitude measuring and displaying devices;
d) For night operations according to visual flight rules, a barometric altitude measuring and displaying device is replaced by a radio altimeter if the aircraft's equipment configuration ensures safe operation."},"translatedText":"Article 1134. Requirements for aircraft and equipment

