Article 1137. Operational procedures and safety instructions for passengers
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for stipulating in the operating manual the operating procedures for single-pilot aircraft operations according to instrument or night flight rules.
2. The exploitation process includes the following contents:
a) Assigning responsibilities of the aircraft commander in single-pilot operations;
b) Procedures for preparing flights, making flight plans, checking weather, checking aeronautical information, checking the technical condition of the aircraft and checking the minimum equipment list;
c) Procedures for using the autopilot system during stages of flight;
d) Procedures for handling when the autopilot system fails or does not work;
d) Procedures for using electronic flight documents, aeronautical charts and shortened documents during flights;
e) Process for managing workload, exchanging information with air traffic control and handling unusual and emergency situations;
g) Procedures for safety instructions for passengers in the absence of flight attendants.
3. For single-pilot operations without flight attendants, the aircraft commander is directly responsible for providing safety instructions to passengers before the flight.
4. The aircraft commander did not provide safety instructions to passengers during the taxiing process and during critical stages of the flight.
5. Aircraft operators may use audio, visual or other electronic means to provide safety instructions to passengers when such instruction method is appropriate to the aircraft type, cabin configuration and expected operations.
