g) Procedures for safety instructions for passengers in the absence of flight attendants.
3. For single-pilot operations without flight attendants, the aircraft commander is directly responsible for providing safety instructions to passengers before the flight.
4. The aircraft commander did not provide safety instructions to passengers during the taxiing process and during critical stages of the flight.
5. Aircraft operators may use audio, visual or other electronic means to provide safety instructions to passengers when such instruction method is appropriate to the aircraft type, cabin configuration and expected operations.
