Article 1139. Engine reliability and maintenance
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring engine reliability and maintenance programs for operating performance class 3 helicopters in meteorological conditions flying with equipment that meets the requirements specified in this Article.
2. Engines used for performance class 3 helicopter operations in instrument flight meteorological conditions must have data showing that the rate of loss of nominal power is less than 01 incident per 100,000 hours of engine operation on the basis of safety risk management procedures.
3. Aircraft operators are responsible for developing, implementing and maintaining an engine trend monitoring program.
4. Dynamic trend monitoring program includes the following contents:
a) Monitor oil consumption in accordance with the recommendations of the organization responsible for designing the type, the engine manufacturer or the corresponding technical documents;
b) Monitor engine condition to detect performance deterioration early and take corrective measures before affecting operational safety;
c) Monitor engine and related system reliability, including operating hours, power loss rates and trends;
d) Store, evaluate and analyze reliability data to take necessary corrective action.
5. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that engines and related systems meet the following requirements to minimize the possibility of damage during flight:
a) For turbine engines, equipped with an automatic ignition system or a continuous ignition system that can be activated manually, unless the type design determines that this system is not necessary;
b) Equipped with a magnetic dust detection system or equivalent system to monitor the engine, auxiliary gearbox and reduction gearbox, accompanied by a warning indicator in the cockpit;
c) The engine is capable of continuing to operate within a power range sufficient to safely complete the flight in the event of a fuel controller failure."},"translatedText":"Article 1139. Engine reliability and maintenance

