Article 1141. Reporting incidents, failures and defects
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for reporting to the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam any incidents, failures, malfunctions or significant defects related to the operation of class 3 performance helicopters in instrument flight meteorological conditions.
2. The report includes the following cases:
a) Loss of engine power, engine failure or reduction in engine power;
b) Failure of the main electrical system or emergency power system;
c) Failure of the autopilot system, stabilization system or area navigation system;
d) Failure of radio altimeter equipment;
d) Failure of the engine fire warning system, magnetic dust detection system or equivalent system;
e) Damage to the fuel controller or power controller;
g) Incident, malfunction or other defect that affects the ability to safely continue flight or make a safe forced landing.
3. Aircraft operators are responsible for storing, evaluating and analyzing reporting data specified in Clause 1 of this Article to identify risk trends and implement necessary risk control measures."},"translatedText":"Article 1141. Reporting incidents, failures and defects

Article 1141. Reporting incidents, failures and defects
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for reporting to the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam any incidents, failures, malfunctions or significant defects related to the operation of class 3 performance helicopters in instrument flight meteorological conditions.
2. The report includes the following cases:
a) Loss of engine power, engine failure or reduction in engine power;
b) Failure of the main electrical system or emergency power system;
c) Failure of the autopilot system, stabilization system or area navigation system;
d) Failure of radio altimeter equipment;
d) Failure of the engine fire warning system, magnetic dust detection system or equivalent system;
e) Damage to the fuel controller or power controller;
g) Incident, malfunction or other defect that affects the ability to safely continue flight or make a safe forced landing.
3. Aircraft operators are responsible for storing, evaluating and analyzing reporting data specified in Clause 1 of this Article to identify risk trends and implement necessary risk control measures."},"1142":{"id":"1142","code":"Điều 1142","title":"Điều 1142. Huấn luyện và kiểm tra năng lực thành viên tổ lái","chapter":"Chương X - KHAI THÁC TRỰC THĂNG TÍNH NĂNG HẠNG 3 TRONG IMC TRONG VẬN TẢI HÀNG KHÔNG THƯƠNG MẠI","partTitle":"Phần XIX - KHAI THÁC ĐẶC BIỆT","partId":"main_part_19","plainText":"Điều 1142. Huấn luyện và kiểm tra năng lực thành viên tổ lái
