Article 1142. Training and checking the capacity of flight crew members
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that flight crew members meet the appropriate flight experience requirements before participating in operating performance class 3 helicopters in instrument flight meteorological conditions.
2. Aircraft operators are responsible for developing, promulgating, implementing and maintaining training and inspection programs for the operation of class 3 performance helicopters in instrument flight meteorological conditions.
3. The training and testing program covers normal, abnormal and emergency procedures related to the operation of performance class 3 helicopters in instrument flight meteorological conditions.
4. The training and testing program includes the following contents:
a) Identify and handle engine damage;
b) Procedures for lowering altitude to perform forced landings in instrument flight meteorological conditions;
c) For single-engine helicopters, procedures for putting the helicopter into stable rotation mode;
d) Use of autopilot system, stabilization system, area navigation system and radio altimeter;
d) Handling failures of the main power system, emergency power system, autopilot system and area navigation system;
e) Selecting a forced landing location and managing the flight trajectory after engine failure;
g) Coordination in the cockpit, workload management and flight crew resource management in instrument flight meteorological conditions.
