3. Trường hợp khai thác trong môi trường không khắc nghiệt, người khai thác tàu bay được lược bỏ các nội dung hướng dẫn liên quan đến trang thiết bị sinh tồn hoặc trang thiết bị khẩn nguy không được yêu cầu trang bị hoặc không áp dụng đối với chuyến bay.</p>","translations":{"en":"Article 1145. Requirements for instructions on using safety equipment for passengers

Article 1145. Requirements for instructions on using safety equipment for passengers
1. Aircraft operators ensure that passengers are instructed in the safe use of equipment before boarding the helicopter by electronic audio-visual means or by flight crew members.
2. Instructions include the following:
a) Use of life jackets and storage location on the helicopter;
b) The use of survival suits, including the requirement to fully zip the suit, wear a hood and wear gloves during takeoff and landing or when requested by the aircraft commander;
c) Use of emergency respiratory support equipment when equipped;
d) Location and method of using emergency exits;
d) Method of activating and using lifeboats;
e) Activation and use of survival equipment;
g) Instructions for boarding and disembarking the helicopter.
3. In case of operating in non-harsh environments, aircraft operators are allowed to omit instructions related to survival equipment or emergency equipment that are not required to be equipped or are not applicable to the flight."},"translatedText":"Article 1145. Requirements for instructions on using safety equipment for passengers

Article 1145. Requirements for instructions on using safety equipment for passengers
1. Aircraft operators ensure that passengers are instructed in the safe use of equipment before boarding the helicopter by electronic audio-visual means or by flight crew members.
2. Instructions include the following:
a) Use of life jackets and storage location on the helicopter;
b) The use of survival suits, including the requirement to fully zip the suit, wear a hood and wear gloves during takeoff and landing or when requested by the aircraft commander;
c) Use of emergency respiratory support equipment when equipped;
d) Location and method of using emergency exits;
d) Method of activating and using lifeboats;
e) Activation and use of survival equipment;
g) Instructions for boarding and disembarking the helicopter.
3. In case of operating in non-harsh environments, aircraft operators are allowed to omit instructions related to survival equipment or emergency equipment that are not required to be equipped or are not applicable to the flight."},"1146":{"id":"1146","code":"Điều 1146","title":"Điều 1146. Yêu cầu đối với việc sử dụng hệ thống điều khiển bay tự động","chapter":"Chương XI - KHAI THÁC TRỰC THĂNG NGOÀI KHƠI","partTitle":"Phần XIX - KHAI THÁC ĐẶC BIỆT","partId":"main_part_19","plainText":"Điều 1146. Yêu cầu đối với việc sử dụng hệ thống điều khiển bay tự động
