Article 1155. Helicopter tracking system
1. Aircraft operators establish and maintain a helicopter tracking and monitoring system for offshore operations in harsh environments from the time the helicopter departs until it arrives at the final destination.
2. The flight is monitored and monitored from the time of takeoff to the time of landing. This function is allowed to be performed by air traffic service providers when operating routes and alternate routes are located entirely within an area or airspace that meets the following requirements:
a) Air traffic monitoring services are provided regularly and supported by an air traffic monitoring system capable of determining aircraft positions at appropriate intervals;
b) The aircraft operator has provided the flight operations assurance service provider with the necessary contact information.
3. In cases not covered by Clause 2 of this Article, the aircraft operator shall establish detailed procedures for the helicopter tracking and monitoring system and handling procedures when deviations or abnormalities occur."},"translatedText":"Article 1155. Helicopter tracking system

