Article 1158. Installation of lifeboats
1. Aircraft operators ensure that installation details on the outer surface of the helicopter body, located within the limited area from 1.22 m (4 ft) above to 0.61 m (2 ft) below the design water level determined according to technical records, do not create a risk of damage to the lifeboat after activation.
2. Details specified in Clause 1 of this Article include:
a) Antenna system;
b) Gas or liquid discharge pipe;
c) The ends of the latches and split latches do not have protective covers;
d) Drainage trough;
d) Details with sharp edges that can cause damage to lifeboats.
3. Determination of potentially dangerous details for the lifeboat is carried out on the basis of the dynamics of the lifeboat in wave conditions, taking into account the maximum sea state limit in which the helicopter can maintain stable buoyancy.
4. Design changes or helicopter configuration adjustments apply risk control measures right from the technical design stage to ensure compatibility with the lifeboat after activation.
5. Aircraft operators develop control procedures in routine maintenance to prevent factors that can affect the operational safety of lifeboats."},"translatedText":"Article 1158. Installation of lifeboats

