Article 1170. Exploitation guidance documents
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for ensuring that risks associated with the helicopter winch operating environment are identified and appropriate mitigation measures are applied through stipulating in the operating manual the contents specified in this Article.
2. Operation manual includes the following contents:
a) Selection criteria, crew composition and training program for flight crew members and technical flight crew members operating helicopter crane operations;
b) Required equipment and dispatch criteria;
c) Minimum mining procedures and standards to ensure that normal, abnormal and emergency mining activities are identified and appropriate risk mitigation measures are applied;
d) Operational performance criteria;
d) Conditions for performing offshore transfers by helicopter crane operations, including limitations related to the movement of vessels or floating structures and wind speeds;
e) Meteorological limits for helicopter crane operations;
g) Criteria for determining the minimum size of the location for carrying out activities appropriate to the type of task;
h) Procedures for determining minimum flight crew composition;
i) Method of keeping records of crew members' winching cycles.
3. The aircraft operator is responsible for providing relevant content in the operating manual to the organization providing or receiving helicopter winch operation services in accordance with the operational tasks.
Part XX
