Article 1186. Basis for approval of changes and environmental protection requirements
1. The person requesting approval of the change must prove that the product after making the change:
a) Meets airworthiness standards under the applicable approval basis. For products that have been issued or recognized by the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam with a Type Certificate or Certificate of conformity to technical standards, the applicable basis for approval is the basis identified in the Type Certificate or Certificate of conformity to that technical standard;
b) Meets environmental protection requirements as prescribed in Article 43 of these Regulations.
2. A change is determined to be an important change when it falls into one of the following cases and the revised standards of the approval basis must only be applied to the contents directly affected by the change, except for the case specified in Point c, Clause 3 of this Article.
a) Change the overall configuration or main design principles of the product;
b) Making the technical assumptions used to determine the basis for approval no longer appropriate;
c) Affects multiple systems or core technical characteristics of the product;
d) Changes that do not fall into the cases specified in this Clause are determined to be unimportant changes.
3. In case compliance with the provisions of Clause 1 of this Article cannot be demonstrated, the applicant may continue to apply the previously applied airworthiness standards if they fall into one of the following cases:
a) Changes are determined to be unimportant changes according to the provisions of Point d, Clause 2 of this Article;
b) Areas, systems, parts or equipment are not affected by the changes;
c) Applying the new standard does not contribute to significantly increasing the safety level of the product or is not technically feasible.
4. For aircraft with a maximum takeoff mass not exceeding 2,722 kg or helicopters not using turbine engines with a maximum takeoff mass not exceeding 1,361 kg, the applicant must demonstrate compliance with the basis of approval stated in the Type Certificate.
5. In case the airworthiness standards specified in Clause 1 of this Article are not sufficient to evaluate the change, the applicant may apply special conditions to ensure an equivalent level of safety.
6. Basis for effective approval:
a) 05 years for large aircraft or large helicopters;
b) 03 years for other products;
c) If the time limit specified in this Clause expires, if the change has not been approved, the basis for approval must be re-determined according to the provisions of Clause 1 of this Article."},"translatedText":"Article 1186. Basis for approval of changes and environmental protection requirements

