Article 1193. Basis for use and installation of aircraft equipment
1. For aircraft equipment in cases where compliance must be demonstrated to ensure flight safety, the applicant is responsible for proving that the equipment meets applicable technical standards or technical features approved or recognized by the Vietnam Aviation Administration for each specific case.
2. Aircraft equipment is allowed to be installed on products that have been issued or recognized with a Type Certificate when they meet one of the following requirements:
a) Approved according to the type design, change design or repair design of the product;
b) Designed and manufactured by a competent organization according to applicable technical standards and recognized by the Vietnam Aviation Administration or a competent aviation authority recognized by the Vietnam Aviation Administration according to Clause 2, Article 8 of Decree No. 223/2026/ND-CP on aircraft and aircraft operations;
c) Belongs to an exempt case as prescribed in this Article.
3. Aircraft equipment not manufactured by the Original Manufacturer (OEM) in the Designing Countries is allowed to be installed on products that have been issued or recognized with a Type Certificate when they simultaneously meet the following requirements:
a) Be eligible for exploitation and labeled according to applicable regulations;
b) Attached is the Certificate of Permission to Operate (CAAV Form 1) or Certificate of Permission to Operate as prescribed by the aviation authorities of the countries mentioned in Clause 2, Article 8 of Decree No. 223/2026/ND-CP on aircraft and aircraft operations;
c) Have approved or recognized design data as a basis for installation;
d) Conforms to the type design configuration or approved modified design;
d) Have documents proving the origin, manufacturing process, maintenance or repair according to applicable regulations.
4. CAAV Form 1 is not required for the following cases:
a) Standard equipment;
b) Equipment installed on light aircraft ELA1 or ELA2 when simultaneously meeting the requirements stated in Clause 5 of this Article;
c) Equipment has deviations from approved or recognized design data but only has a negligible impact on flight safety and is allowed to be used according to approved or recognized standards, design data or technical documents. Where the Maintenance of Airworthiness Instructions (ICA) is applicable, this document must specify the necessary testing measures to confirm the safe installation and operation of the equipment;
d) Equipment used when making changes to standards or repairing standards, provided that such equipment is identified in technical standards or design data that have been issued, approved or recognized. The installer shall verify within the requirements and limitations specified in that standard or technical data and shall not make his or her own determination or conclusion about the degree of safety impact beyond the approved or recognized scope.
5. Requirements for equipment to be allowed to be installed on aircraft of type ELA1 or ELA2:
a) It is not a detail that has a limited lifespan;
b) Not part of the main structure;
c) Not part of the flight control system;
d) Not an equipment that has a material impact on flight safety;
d) Identified for installation on a specific aircraft;
e) There is appropriate technical data as a basis for installation and is recorded in the aircraft's technical records;
g) Installation is carried out and certified by an approved maintenance organization or authorized personnel;
h) Only applicable to aircraft not performing commercial operations.
6. Equipment declared by the aeronautical authority of the State of design to be exempt from the requirement for airworthiness approval may be used according to the scope and conditions of the respective exemption.
7. Equipment that is a small item belonging to a larger assembly specified in Clause 4 of this Article is allowed to be installed when it simultaneously meets the following requirements:
a) Does not affect flight safety;
b) It is not a detail that has a limited lifespan;
c) Not part of the main structure or flight control system;
d) Meet applicable material standards or technical standards;
d) Have documents proving origin and full traceability."},"translatedText":"Article 1193. Basis for use and installation of aircraft equipment

