Article 1196. Product identification data
1. Removal, change or installation of identification information specified in Clause 1, Article 1195 of these Regulations on aircraft, engines, propellers, propeller blades or propeller cones must only be carried out according to design data, maintenance data or technical documents approved by the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam, or recognized according to applicable regulations.
2. Organizations and individuals performing maintenance according to the provisions of these Regulations are allowed to:
a) Remove, change or install identification information specified in Clause 1, Article 1195 of these Regulations when necessary to perform maintenance work according to approved or accepted technical data;
b) Remove the identification plate specified in Article 1195 of these Regulations when necessary to perform maintenance work.
3. The identification plate removed as prescribed in Point b, Clause 2 of this Article may only be reinstalled on the aircraft itself, the engine, propeller, propeller blade or the cone of the propeller that has been removed; It is strictly prohibited to install such identification plate on other products."},"translatedText":"Article 1196. Product identification data

Article 1196. Product identification data
