Article 1202. Aircraft testing
1. The manufacturer of an aircraft required by this Chapter shall develop and implement ground and flight test procedures to confirm that the aircraft is manufactured in accordance with applicable design data and is in a safe operating condition.
2. The testing process must ensure assessment and confirmation of the following contents:
a) Functions and control capabilities of aircraft equipment;
b) Characteristics and flight performance of aircraft products and equipment within the approved scope of operations;
c) Correct operation of systems, equipment and facilities installed on the aircraft;
d) Full installation of signs, signs, exploitation documents and mandatory equipment according to applicable design data;
d) Operational characteristics of aircraft on the ground;
e) Other test requirements necessary to confirm the aircraft's compliance with applicable design data."},"translatedText":"Article 1202. Aircraft testing

