Article 1209. Notice requirements differ from ICAO standards
1. Foreign aircraft operators operating in Vietnam with differences compared to ICAO standards must notify the Vietnam Aviation Administration of the differences, including:
a) Content different from ICAO standards;
b) Measures to ensure equivalent levels of safety.
2. Foreign aircraft operators must notify the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam when there are changes related to the Aircraft Operator Certificate issued by the operator's national authorities.
