Article 1222. General provisions
1. The commander of the aircraft must ensure that all flight crew members understand and comply with relevant laws, regulations and procedures of the country the aircraft is flying through during the performance of their duties.
2. The aircraft commander is responsible for the task of controlling and operating the flight.
3. If an emergency situation occurs that threatens the safety and security of the flight, forcing the aircraft commander to take action that violates the regulations of the relevant country, the aircraft commander must immediately notify the authorities of that country within ten days. In case of request, the aircraft commander must submit a report on the violation to the aviation authorities of that country. The aircraft commander must send a copy of the report to the country of registration of the aircraft.
4. The aircraft commander must have on board the aircraft information about search and rescue services related to the area over which the aircraft flies.
5. The aircraft commander must ensure that flight crew members are able to speak and understand the language used in aviation radio communications.
6. Persons operating aircraft with complex engine aircraft must:
a) Provide the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam with a Declaration containing relevant information before starting operations according to the form specified in Appendix LIX issued with this Regulation;
b) Maintain compliance with applicable requirements and the information provided in the statement;
c) Notify the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam when terminating operations or when there are changes related to the content of the Declaration."},"translatedText":"Article 1222. General provisions

