Article 1223. Documents to carry on flights
1. Organizations and individuals must ensure that the documents they carry on their flights are as follows:
a) Documents as prescribed in Article 44 of Decree No. 223/2026/ND-CP on aircraft and aircraft operations;
b) Aircraft technical logbook;
c) Flight instruction documents, operation instructions documents;
d) Minimum equipment list;
d) Air traffic flight plan;
e) Operational flight plan;
g) Documents summarizing aviation service information, NOTAMS and meteorological information;
h) Weight profile and center of gravity balance of the aircraft;
i) Aeronautical maps and charts serving expected routes and possible diversion routes;
k) Aircraft insurance certificate;
l) Information about search and rescue services in areas along the flight itinerary;
m) Visual signaling procedures and information for intercepting aircraft and intercepted aircraft;
n) Summary of agreement, if applicable;
o) Other documents and records required by the aviation authorities of the countries related to the expected flight;
p) Other documents and records as prescribed by Vietnamese law on customs.
2. The summary of the agreement is the original or a certified copy according to the provisions of Vietnamese law on clerical work."},"translatedText":"Article 1223. Documents to carry on flights

