Article 1224. Control and administration of exploitation
1. For general aviation activities using small aircraft, the aircraft commander is responsible for controlling flight operations.
2. For general aviation operations using large aircraft or turbojet aircraft:
a) Aircraft operators must establish and maintain an operations management system, described in the operations manual, including the roles, responsibilities and authority of individuals participating in operations operations.
b) The aircraft commander is responsible for controlling flight operations.
3. Aircraft operators must keep operational records for each flight for a minimum period of 03 months from the date of flight, records include:
a) Implemented air traffic flight plan;
b) Pre-flight planning documents;
c) Documents calculating mass, balancing the center of gravity and aircraft features;
d) Journey log, technical logbook related to the flight.
