Article 1235. Contents of training and testing of aircraft pilots
1. Flight crew resource management training
a) Before performing operational tasks, flight crew members must be trained in flight crew resource management in accordance with their assigned positions and tasks as prescribed in the operational manual;
b) The content of flight crew resource management training must be implemented in the aircraft type or class conversion training program, periodic training and main pilot upgrade training.
2. Training for aircraft operator conversion
a) Flight crew members must complete the aircraft operator conversion training course before performing independent duties in case of changing aircraft type or class or when changing aircraft operators;
b) The aircraft operator conversion training course must include training content on equipment installed on the aircraft related to the duties of flight crew members.
3. Differentiation training, familiarization, equipment and method training
a) Flight crew members must complete differentiation training or aircraft familiarization training;
b) Flight crew members must complete training on equipment and procedures when there is a change in equipment or a change in procedures that requires additional knowledge for the types or variants of aircraft being operated;
c) Training program documents must specify situations requiring differential training, familiarization training or training on equipment and procedures.
4. Periodic training and testing
a) Flight crew members must complete periodic training within 12 months including flight training and ground training appropriate to the type or variant of aircraft and related equipment of the aircraft that the flight crew member operates, including training on the location and use of safety and emergency equipment equipped on the aircraft;
b) Flight crew members must be periodically tested to demonstrate their ability to perform normal, abnormal and emergency flight procedures.
5. Flight crew members assigned to perform tasks at both driver's seat positions must complete the training and testing program as prescribed in the operating manual.
6. Flight crew members operating more than one type or variant of aircraft shall comply with the requirements set forth in this Article for each aircraft type or variant, unless a reduction in current training, testing and experience is identified in operational fitness data or equivalent documentation approved by the State responsible for design."},"translatedText":"Article 1235. Contents of training and testing of aircraft pilots

