Article 1236. Organization of training and testing of aircraft pilots
1. The content of training, testing and evaluation of aircraft pilots must be carried out in accordance with the training program and curriculum developed by the aircraft operator in the Operational Instructions Document.
2. When developing training programs and textbooks, aircraft operators must ensure that they include the relevant content specified in operational appropriate data or equivalent documents approved by the State responsible for aircraft design.
