2.31.9	Requirements for CPDLC and ADS-C Maintenance Training
a)	The technical staff must be trained in CPDLC and ADS-C maintenance, including initial training and continuation training.
b)	The CPDLC and ADS-C training program is approved by CAAV during the application for CPDLC and ADS-C operation approval.
2.31.10	Maintenance Procedures
	Contracted AMO is responsible for ensuring
a)	Control of maintenance CPDLC/ADS-C procedures:
1)	The contracted AMO is responsible for implementing CPDLC/ADS-C maintenance procedures.
2)	They need to check the status of CPDLC/ADS-C before aircraft are in operation, including reports from pilots about failing equipment and CPDLC/ADS-C systems, ensuring the aircraft has no CPDLC or ADS-C - related problems, and closing any related defects.
b)	Controlling and monitoring the status of the CPDLS or ADS-C systems installed the aircraft:
1)	MOC shall monitor the status of CPDLC/ADS-C systems on the aircraft based on criteria set out in documents such as MEL (Minimum Equipment List), FCOM (Flight Crew Operations Manual), QRH (Quick Reference Handbook), and others.
2)	Certifying staff are responsible for determining whether the CPDLC/ADS-C system on the aircraft can be used or not.
	Downgrade of CPDLC/ADS-C
If a CPDLC/ADS-C System defect cannot be corrected before aircraft dispatch, do the following:
a)	Apply the MEL in accordance with MME 2.1.2.3 and add phrase “NON-CPDLC/ADS-C OPERATION” into the ADD raised;
b)	Add the phrase “NON – CPDLC/ADS-C OPERATION” in the Technical Log after the statement about defect rectification;
c)	Open an NTC as per a standard procedure, ensuring the phrase “NON-CPDLC/ADS-C OPERATION” is included (Ref. MME.2.1.2.3);
d)	Brief Flight Crew of any possible performance limitations resulting from the CPDLC and ADS-C system defect;
e)	CRS shall immediately notify MOC about the defect and CPDLC/ADS-C downgrade and which MEL that has been applied;
f)	MOC shall immediately inform OMC about this downgraded CPDLC/ADS-C status to ensure that flight operations with CPDLC/ADS-C limitation are coordinated accordingly.
	Upgrade of CPDLC/ADS-C System
When the CPDLC/ADS-C - related defect has been corrected and the aircraft can be verified to return to the CPDLC/ADS-C operation for the next flight, do the following:
a)	CRS shall clear the defect raised IAW MEL and make a clear statement "A/C RETURN TO CPDLC/ADS-C OPERATION" in the Technical Log to inform the Flight Crew or Maintenance personnel about this upgraded CPDLC and ADS-C status;
b)	Clear the related NTC that was raised previously;
c)	CRS shall immediately inform MOC about defect rectification and upgraded CPDLC/ADS-C status.
d)	MOC shall then immediately notify OMC about the CPDLC/ADS-C upgrade to ensure that flight operations without CPDLC/ADS-C limitation are coordinated accordingly.
