2.32.1	Objective
This maintenance procedure ensures the effective maintenance and configuration control of systems required for operation in the North Atlantic High-Level Airspace (NAT HLA) under “NAT Without Restrictions” conditions.
2.32.2	Scope
This procedure applies to all VJC A330 aircraft intended to operate in NAT HLA (MNPS), ensuring that required aircraft systems meet the standards set out by CAAV (Ref. AC 10-006), and ICAO (Ref. NAT Doc 007) for NAT HLA operations without RESTRICTIONS.
2.32.3	References
a)	ICAO NAT Doc 007
b)	ICAO Doc 9574 (RVSM MASPS)
c)	CAAV VAR Part 6
d)	CAAV AC 10-006
e)	Airbus A330 AFM
f)	VJC MEL
g)	VJC Datalink Manual
2.32.4	Responsibilities
The engineering Director is responsible for ensuring fleet-wide compliance with the NAT HLA system configuration and procedures.
The training Department is responsible for developing NAT HLA maintenance training content and delivering it to VJC technical personnel, AMO staff, and contracted organizations.
TQA is responsible for reviewing NAT HLA maintenance records, instructor authorizations, and procedure compliance.
Contracted AMO is responsible for the implementation and execution of all NAT HLA maintenance in accordance with approved instructions and compliance requirements.
FOE is responsible for updating the MEL items related to NAT HLA operations.
2.32.5	System Description
According to ICAO NAT Doc 007 and CAAV AC 10-006, to qualify for NAT HLA without RESTRICTIONS, A330 aircraft must be equipped with and approved for the following.
a)	The standard equipment for NAT HLA without RESTRICTION operations:
1)	VHF radios
2)	Dual LRCS (2 HF radios)
3)	SATCOM Data
4)	ADS-B OUT (ES)
5)	Dual LRNS (GPS/IRS)
6)	SSR Mode A/C transponder
7)	Traffic Collision Avoidance System (TCAS) 7.1
b)	The procedures with respect to the following minimum communication and navigation performance to conduct NAT HLA operations:
1)	RVSM between FL285 and FL420 (Refer to MME 2.17)
2)	RNP4 and RNP2 navigation (Refer to MME 2.23)
3)	CPDLC and ADS-C (Refer to MME 2.31)
4)	PBCS (Refer to MME 2.33)
