d)	All NAT HLA required systems must be functionally tested after replacement.
2.32.9	NAT HLA Maintenance Training Requirements
a)	The technical staff must be trained in NAT HLA maintenance, including initial training and continuation training.
b)	The NAT HLA training program is approved by CAAV during the application for NAT HLA operation approval.
2.32.10	Maintenance Procedures
	Maintenance Control and Monitoring
a)	AMO responsibilities:
	Maintain NAT HLA systems in accordance with the approved maintenance documents such as MMEL, AMM, and IPC.
	Monitor equipment status and close any ADDs/NAT-related faults before the dispatch for NAT HLA operation.
b)	MOC responsibilities:
	Monitor the status of NAT HLA capability on the VJC A330 fleet.
	Validate whether a flight can proceed through NAT HLA based on MEL limitations.
	Downgrade from NAT HLA Eligibility
If the aircraft cannot meet NAT HLA eligibility, do the following:
a)	Apply the MEL in accordance with MME 2.1.2.3, and add the phrase “NON-NAT HLA OPERATION” into the ADD raised;
b)	Add the phrase “NON – NAT HLA OPERATION” into the Technical Log after the statement about defect rectification;
c)	Open an NTC as per a standard procedure, ensuring the phrase “NON-NAT HLA OPERATION” is included (Ref. MME.2.1.2.3);
d)	Brief Flight Crew of any possible performance limitations resulting from the NAT HLA system defect;
e)	CRS shall immediately notify MOC about the defect and NAT HLA downgrade and which MEL item has been applied;
f)	MOC shall immediately inform OMC about this downgraded NAT HLA status to ensure that flight operations with NAT HLA limitation are coordinated accordingly.
	Upgrade to NAT HLA Eligibility
When the NAT HLA defect has been corrected and the aircraft can be verified to return to the NAT HLA operation for the next flight, do the following:
a)	CRS shall clear the defect raised IAW MEL and make a clear statement "A/C RETURN TO NAT HLA OPERATION" in the Technical Log to inform the Flight Crew or Maintenance personnel about this upgraded NAT HLA status;
b)	Clear the related NTC that was raised previously;
c)	CRS shall immediately inform MOC about defect rectification and upgraded NAT HLA status.
d)	MOC shall then immediately notify OMC about the NAT HLA upgrade to ensure that flight operations without NAT HLA limitation are coordinated accordingly.
