b)	The equipment installed on the aircraft must comply with the Airbus A330 IPC for PBCS eligibility and high reliability.
c)	The relevant software and database such as all the ATSU software and the database used for the PBCS application must be installed in accordance with Airbus A330 IPC and AMM during the PBCS equipment replacement.
d)	Technical Services and Planning Departments monitor AD, SB, and other documents from manufacturers related to PBCS operation and accordingly modify the PBCS maintenance program when necessary. Technical Services and Planning Departments also need to update the PBCS maintenance procedure and inform the Flight Operations Division, Supply Department, Technical Quality Assurance Department, Flight Ops Division, and contracted maintenance organizations about these modifications.
e)	The current configuration of PBCS capability in an aircraft’s avionics system shall be reported to CAAV inspectors when requested.
2.33.7	PBCS Maintenance Program
a)	Airbus aircraft do not require special maintenance for PBCS equipment.
b)	The equipment related to this program is maintained IAW the approved AMP (MPD) if applicable.
2.33.8	Equipment Inspection and Quality Monitoring
The devices and tools used to maintain the related PBCS system must meet the following requirements:
a)	Use only test equipment specified in approved manuals.
b)	Ensure periodic calibration of test equipment.
c)	Perform calibration in accordance with the manufacturer’s recommendations.
d)	Comply with all relevant technical procedures.
2.33.9	Requirements for PBCS Maintenance Training
a)	The technical staff must be trained in PBCS maintenance, including initial training and continuation training.
b)	The PBCS training program is approved by CAAV during the application for PBCS operation approval.
2.33.10	Maintenance Procedures
	Downgrade of PBCS Capability
If the aircraft cannot meet PBCS standards (RCP240 or RSP180), do the following:
a)	Apply the MEL in accordance with MME 2.1.2.3, and add the phrase “NON-PBCS OPERATION” into the ADD raised;
b)	Add the phrase “NON – PBCS OPERATION” into the Technical Log after the statement about defect rectification;
c)	Open an NTC as per a standard procedure, ensuring the phrase “NON-PBCS OPERATION” is included (Ref. MME.2.1.2.3);
d)	Brief Flight Crew on any possible performance limitations resulting from the CPDLC system defect;
e)	CRS shall immediately notify MOC about the defect and PBCS downgrade, and which MEL has been applied;
f)	MOC shall immediately inform OMC about this downgraded PBCS status to ensure that flight operations with PBCS limitation are coordinated accordingly.
	Upgrade of PBCS System
If the PBCS-related defect has been corrected and the aircraft can be verified to be returned to the PBCS operation for the next flight, do the following:
a)	CRS shall clear the defect raised IAW MEL and make a clear statement "A/C RETURN TO PBCS OPERATION" in the Technical Log to inform the Flight Crew or Maintenance personnel about this upgraded PBCS status;
b)	Clear the related NTC that was raised previously;
c)	CRS shall immediately inform MOC about defect rectification and the upgraded PBCS status;
d)	MOC shall then immediately notify OMC about the PBCS upgrade to ensure that flight operations without PBCS limitation are coordinated accordingly.
