2.33.12	PBCS monitoring process
Every three months, Avionics TSEs shall:
1)	Log in to https://www.fans-cra.com/performance/list/
2)	Download and review the latest RCP/RSP performance data for VJC’s aircraft.
3)	Identify any aircraft listed as non-compliant with either RCP 240 or RSP 180
Note: Any the result below 95% is considered non-compliant with PBCS criteria
4)	If an aircraft is identified as non-compliant, the Avionics TSE shall coordinate with MOC and contracted AMOs to downgrade its PBCS capability in accordance with MME 2.33.10.1
5)	If the PBCS-related defect has been corrected and the aircraft can be verified to be returned to the PBCS operation for the next flight IAW MME 2.33.10.2
Additionally, if the Avionics TSEs are notified or detect non-compliance with datalink performance requirements (RCP/RSP specifications) based on reports sent from VJC SQA, they shall initiate investigations involving the PBCS stakeholders, including aircraft manufacturers such as Airbus, and CSPs in order to determine the root cause of this underperformance issue and take corrective actions or define mitigation plans accordingly.
