Whenever the management system for maintenance operations involves another organization's management system (e.g. the case of continuing airworthiness management ensured by an organization external to the operator but belonging to the same airline business group the operator is part of) particular attention to the harmonization of the two management systems is necessary. In such cases, the operator is expected to arrange for the auditing appropriate logistic required to demonstrate and assess that the management systems are harmonized with each other.
